\h Ezekiel
\toc1 The Book of Ezekiel
\toc2 Ezekiel
\toc3 Ezk
\mt1 Ezekiel
\c 1
\p
\v 1 And it was in the thirtieth year—on the fourth {month}, on the fifth day of the month—and I {was} among the exiles along the river of Kebar. The heavens opened, and I saw visions of God.
\v 2 On the fifth {day} of the month—it {was} the fifth year of the exile of King Jehoiachin—
\v 3 the word of Yahweh, being, was to Ezekiel, son of Buzi, the priest, in the land of the Chaldeans on the river of Kebar. And it was on him there, the hand of Yahweh.
\b
\p
\v 4 Then I saw, and behold, a wind of storm, coming from the north, a great cloud and fire, catching itself. And brightness {was} to it all around, and from the midst of it {was} like the eye of metal from the midst of the fire.
\v 5 And in the midst of it {was} the likeness of four beings. And this {was} their appearance—the likeness of a man {belonged} to them,
\v 6 but four faces {belonged} to each one, and four wings {belonged} to each one of them.
\v 7 And their two feet {were} straight feet, but a palm of their two feet {were} like a palm of a foot of a calf and gleaming like an eye of polished bronze.
\v 8 And his hand {was} a man, from under their wings on four of their four sides. And their faces and their wings of the four of them—
\v 9 their wings were each joining to its sister; they did not turn as they went; each went toward his faces.
\b
\v 10 And the likeness of their faces: the face of a man, and the face of a lion to the right {belonged} to the four of them, and the face of an ox from the left {belonged} to the four of them, and the face of an eagle {belonged} to the four of them.
\v 11 So, their faces. And their wings were spread from above. Of each {one}, two were joining each, and two were covering their bodies.
\v 12 And each {one}, its face went forward. Toward wherever the spirit was there to go, they went; they did not turn as they went.
\v 13 And the likeness of the beings—their appearance {was} like coals of burning fire, like the appearance of torches. It {was} moving about between the beings and {was} a brightness of the fire, and, from the fire, lightning was coming forth.
\v 14 And the beings, by running and returning, {were} like the appearance of the lightning strike.
\b
\p
\v 15 Then I saw the beings, and behold, one wheel on the ground beside the beings, of four of its faces.
\v 16 The appearance of the wheels and their works {was} like an eye of topaz, and the likeness of one {belonged} to the four of them. And their appearance and their works—it was just like the wheel in the midst of the wheel.
\v 17 Toward four of their sides, when they went, they went; they did not turn when they went.
\v 18 And their rims—and height {belonged} to them, and fear {belonged} to them. And the rims {were} full of eyes all around of the four of them.
\b
\v 19 And when the beings went, the wheels went beside them. And when the beings rose from on the ground, the wheels rose.
\v 20 Toward wherever the spirit was there to go, they went—the spirit {was} there to go. And the wheels ascended beside them, for the spirit of the beings {was} in the wheels.
\v 21 When they went, they went; and when they stood, they stood; and when they ascended from on the ground, the wheels ascended beside them, because the spirit of the beings {was} in the wheels.
\b
\p
\v 22 And the likeness over the heads of the beings {was} a vault, like the eye of the fearsome ice, being stretched over their heads from above.
\v 23 And under the vault, their wings {were} straight, each to its sister. Of each, two were covering themselves; and of each, two were covering themselves, their bodies.
\v 24 Then, I heard the sound of their wings—like a sound of many waters, like a sound of the Almighty when they moved, like a sound of a crowd, like a sound of an army. When they stood, their wings slackened.
\b
\v 25 And it was, a voice from above the dome that {was} over their head; when they stood, their wings slackened.
\p
\v 26 And from above the vault that {was} over their head, like the appearance of a stone of sapphire, {was} the likeness of a throne, and on the likeness of the throne {was} a likeness, like the appearance of a man on it from above.
\v 27 And I saw {something} like the eye of metal, like the appearance of fire—a house {belonged} to it all around—from the appearance of his waist and upwards. And from the appearance of his waist and downward, I saw {something} like the appearance of fire. And brightness {belonged} to it all around,
\v 28 like the appearance of a rainbow that is in a cloud on a day of the rain. Thus {was} the appearance of the brightness all around. It {was} the appearance of the likeness of the glory of Yahweh. And I saw, and I fell on my face, and I heard a voice speaking.
\c 2
\p
\v 1 Then he said to me, “Son of man, stand on your feet, so that I might speak to you.”
\v 2 And the Spirit entered into me when he spoke to me, and it made me stand on my feet. Then I heard {one} speaking to me.
\b
\v 3 And he said to me, “Son of man, I am sending you to the sons of Israel, to rebellious nations that have rebelled against me. They and their fathers have revolted against me up to the bone of this day.
\v 4 And the sons {are} hard of face and strong of heart. I am sending you to them, and you will say to them, ‘Thus says the Lord Yahweh.’
\v 5 But they—whether they listen or whether they refuse, for a house of rebellion {are} they—but they will know that a prophet is in their midst.
\p
\v 6 But you, son of man—you shall not fear because of them, and because of their words, you shall not fear. Even though briers and thorns {are} to you, and with scorpions you are dwelling—because of their words, you shall not fear; and from their faces you shall not be dismayed, for they {are} a house of rebellion.
\v 7 But you will speak my words to them—whether they listen or whether they refuse, because they are a rebellion.
\p
\v 8 But you, son of man, listen to that which I am speaking to you. You shall not be rebellious, like the house of rebellion. Open your mouth, and eat that which I am giving to you.”
\b
\p
\v 9 And I saw, and behold, a hand was being sent to me. And behold, in it, a scroll of writing.
\v 10 And he spread it out before me, and it was written, face and back, and written on it were laments and mourning and woe.
\c 3
\p
\v 1 Then he said to me, “Son of man, that which you have found, eat. Eat that scroll, and go, speak to the house of Israel.”
\v 2 So I opened my mouth, and he made me eat that scroll.
\p
\v 3 And he said to me, “Son of man, you shall make your belly eat, and you shall fill your stomach {with} that scroll that I am giving to you.” So I ate it, and it was, in my mouth, like honey—sweet.
\p
\v 4 And he said to me, “Son of man, come; go to the house of Israel, and you shall speak with my words to them,
\v 5 for not to a people deep of lip and heavy of tongue are you being sent, {but} to the house of Israel—
\v 6 not to many peoples, deep of lip or heavy of tongue, that you do not hear their words. Surely, not to them did I send you. They, they would have listened to you.
\v 7 But the house of Israel will not be willing to listen to you, for they are not willing to listen to me, for all the house of Israel—they {are} strong of forehead and hard of heart.
\v 8 Behold! I have made your face strong as beside their faces and your forehead hard as beside their foreheads.
\v 9 As a thorn harder than flint, I have made your forehead. You shall not fear them, and you shall not be dismayed from their faces, for they {are} a house of rebellion.”
\b
\p
\v 10 And he said to me, “Son of man, all the words that I am speaking to you—take {them} into your heart, and, in your ears, listen {to them}.
\v 11 And come, go to the exiles, to the sons of your people, and you shall speak to them, and you shall say to them, ‘Thus says the Lord Yahweh,’ whether they listen or whether they refuse.”
\b
\p
\v 12 Then the Spirit lifted me, and I heard behind me a sound of a great earthquake—“Blessed be the glory of Yahweh from his place!”—
\v 13 and the sound of the wings of the living beings, each brushing its sister, and the sound of the wheels beside them, and a sound of a great earthquake.
\v 14 And the Spirit lifted me and took me, and I went bitterly in the heat of my spirit, and the hand of Yahweh was strong on me.
\v 15 So I came to the exiles {at} Tel Aviv, the ones dwelling along the river of Kebar, and who were sitting there. And I sat there {for} seven days, appalled in their midst.
\p
\v 16 And it was, {at} the end of seven days, and it was, the word of Yahweh {was} to me, saying,
\v 17 “Son of man, a watchman I have made you for the house of Israel. So you shall hear a word from my mouth, and you shall warn them from it.
\v 18 When I say to the wicked, ‘You will certainly die,’ and you do not warn him, and you do not speak to warn {the} wicked from his wicked way, so that he might live—he, wicked, he will die in his iniquity, but his blood from your hand I will seek.
\v 19 But you—when you warn {the} wicked, and he does not turn from his wickedness or from his wicked way, he, he will die in his iniquity; but you—your life you will have rescued.
\b
\p
\v 20 But when {the} righteous turns from his righteousness and does injustice, and I put an obstacle before him, he, he will die. If you did not warn him, in his sin he will die, and his righteousness that he did will not be remembered but his blood from your hand I will seek.
\v 21 But you—when you warn him, {the} righteous—without sinning {is} {the} righteous, and he, he does not sin, his life will be, because he was warned. But you—your life you will have rescued.”
\b
\p
\v 22 So, on me there was the hand of Yahweh. And he said to me, “Rise! Go out to the valley, and there I will speak {to} you.”
\v 23 I arose, and I went out to the valley, and behold!—there, the glory of Yahweh was standing, like the glory that I saw along the river of Kebar. And I fell on my face.
\p
\v 24 Then the Spirit came into me, and it made me stand on my feet. And he spoke {to} me, and he said to me, “Go, shut yourself in the midst of your house.
\v 25 But you, son of man—behold! They will put on you ropes, and they will bind you with them, and you will not go out in their midst.
\v 26 And your tongue, I will make cling to your palate, and you will be mute, and you will not be to them, to a man, a reprover, for they {are} a house of rebellion.
\v 27 And when I speak {to} you, I will open your mouth, and you will say to them, ‘Thus says the Lord Yahweh!’ The {one} hearing will hear; the {one} refusing will refuse, for they are a rebellious house!”
\c 4
\p
\v 1 “But you, son of man, take for yourself a brick, and you shall put it to your face. Then you shall inscribe on it a city, Jerusalem.
\v 2 Then, you shall place a siege against it, and you shall build siege walls against it, and you shall pour out a mound against it. And you shall place camps against it, and you shall put battering rams against it, all around.
\v 3 But you—take for yourself a griddle of iron, and you shall put it {as} a wall of iron, between you and between the city. Then you shall make firm your face to it, and it will be in the siege, and you shall lay siege against it. A sign {is} this for the house of Israel.
\p
\v 4 But you—lie on your left side, and you shall put the iniquity of the house of Israel on it. {For} the number of days that you shall lie on it, you will bear their iniquity.
\v 5 And I myself will give to you the years of their iniquity {as} the number of days: 390 days. And you shall bear the iniquity of the house of Israel.
\p
\v 6 And {when} you have completed these {days}, then you shall lie on your right side a second time, and you shall bear the iniquity of the house of Judah: 40 days—a day for a year, a day for a year, I give to you.
\v 7 And to the siege of Jerusalem, you shall make firm your face, and your arm bared. And you shall prophesy against it.
\v 8 And behold!—I am putting on you ropes, and you will not turn from your side to your side until you have completed the days of your siege.
\p
\v 9 But you—take for yourself wheat and barley and beans and lentils and millet and rye, and you shall put them in one vessel, and you shall make them for yourself into bread {for} the number of the days that you are lying on your side—390 days, you shall eat it.
\v 10 And your food that you will eat {shall be}, by weight, twenty shekels per day. From time to time, you shall eat it.
\v 11 And water—by measure, you shall drink a sixth {of} a hin. From time to time, you shall drink.
\v 12 And a cake of barley, you shall eat it. But it—in the dung of the excrement of man, you shall bake it to their eyes.”
\p
\v 13 And Yahweh said, “Like thus, the sons of Israel will eat their unclean bread among the nations that I will banish them there.”
\p
\v 14 But I said, “Ah, Lord Yahweh! Behold! My life has not been made unclean, and carcass or carrion I have not eaten, from my youth until now, and meat of defilement has not entered into my mouth!”
\p
\v 15 And he said to me, “Look—I am giving to you the droppings of cattle instead of the excrement of man. And you shall make your bread over them.”
\p
\v 16 And he said to me, “Son of man—behold me breaking the staff of bread in Jerusalem, and they will eat bread by weight and with anxiety; and water, by measure and in horror, they will drink,
\v 17 because they will lack bread and water. A man and his brother will be dismayed, and they will rot in their iniquity.”
\c 5
\p
\v 1 “But you, son of man—take for yourself a sharp sword. {As} a knife of the barbers, you shall take it for yourself, and you shall pass {it} over your head and over your beard. And you shall take for yourself balances of weight, and you shall divide them.
\v 2 A third, you shall burn in the fire in the midst of the city when the days of the siege are full. And you shall take the third, and you shall strike {it} with the sword all around it, and the third you shall scatter to the wind, and a sword I will empty after them.
\v 3 But you shall take from there a small {amount} in number, and you shall bind them on your {two} edges.
\v 4 And some of them you shall again take, and you shall throw them into the midst of the fire, and you shall burn them in the fire. From it, a fire will go out to all the house of Israel.
\v 5 Thus says the Lord Yahweh, ‘This {is} Jerusalem; in the midst of the nations, I have placed her, and all around her {are} lands.
\v 6 But she has rebelled {against} my judgments with wickedness more than the nations, and {against} my statutes more than the lands that {are} all around her. For they have rejected my judgments, and my statutes—they have not walked in them.’
\p
\v 7 Therefore, thus says the Lord Yahweh, ‘Because of your arrogance, more than the nations that {are} all around you—in my statutes, you have not walked, and my judgments you have not done, and according to the customs of the nations that {are} all around you, you have not done’—
\v 8 therefore, thus says the Lord Yahweh, ‘Look {at} me, against you—even me! And I will do judgments in your midst to the eyes of the nations.
\v 9 And I will do with you that which I have not done and that which I will not do like it again, on account of all your abominations.
\v 10 Therefore, fathers will eat sons in your midst, and sons will eat their fathers. And I will do with you judgments, and I will sow all your remainder to every wind.
\p
\v 11 Therefore, the life {of} me’—a declaration of the Lord Yahweh—‘certainly because my sanctuary you have made unclean with all your abhorrences and with all your abominations, and so I myself will reduce, and my eye will not have pity, and even I myself will not spare.
\v 12 A third of you by the plague will die, or by the famine they will be finished in your midst. And a third by the sword will fall all around you. And a third to every wind I will scatter, and a sword I will empty after them.
\p
\v 13 Then my nose will be finished, and I will pacify my heat among them, and I will soothe myself. Then they will know that I, Yahweh, have spoken in my jealousy when I have completed my heat among them.
\v 14 And I will make you into a desolation and into a reproach among the nations that {are} all around you, to the eyes of everyone passing by.
\v 15 So it will become a reproach and a taunt, a warning and a horror to the nations that {are} all around you, when I do among you my judgments with nose and with heat and with reprimands of heat. I, Yahweh, have spoken!
\v 16 When I send out the disastrous arrows of the famine among them—which will become destruction, which I will send them to destroy you—then I will increase the famine against you, and I will break for you {the} staff of bread.
\v 17 So I will send against you famine and disastrous creatures, and they will bereave you, and plague and blood will pass through you, and a sword I will bring against you. I, Yahweh, have spoken!’”
\c 6
\p
\v 1 And the word of Yahweh was to me, saying,
\v 2 “Son of man, set your face to the mountains of Israel and prophesy to them.
\v 3 And you shall say, ‘Mountains of Israel, hear the word of the Lord Yahweh! Thus says the Lord Yahweh to the mountains and to the hills, to the streambeds and to the valleys, “Look {at} me! I am bringing against you a sword, and I will destroy your high places.
\v 4 Then your sacrificial altars will become desolate, and your incense altars will be broken. And I will throw down your slain in front of your idols.
\v 5 I will place the corpses of the sons of Israel in front of their idols, and I will scatter your bones all around your sacrificial altars.
\v 6 In all your dwellings, the cities will dry up, and the high places will be desolate, so that your sacrificial altars will be dried up and desolate. Then your idols will be broken and disappear, and your incense altars will be hewn, and your works will be annihilated.
\v 7 And the slain will fall in your midst, and you will know that I {am} Yahweh.
\p
\v 8 But I will reserve {some}, when you become survivors of a sword among the nations, when you are scattered among the lands.
\v 9 Then your survivors will remember me among the nations where they were deported there—that I was shattered {by} their heart, the prostituting {one}, which turned away from me, and {by} their eyes, the ones prostituting after their idols. Then they will feel loathing in their faces toward the evils that they did by all their abominations.
\v 10 And they will know that I {am} Yahweh. {It was} not for nothing {that} I spoke to do to them this disaster.”
\v 11 Thus says the Lord Yahweh, “Strike with your palms and stomp with your foot! And say, ‘Ah!’ toward all the abominations of the evils of the house of Israel! For by the sword, by the famine, and by the plague, they will fall.
\v 12 The remote {one}—by the plague, he will die; and the near {one}—by the sword, he will fall; and the remaining {one} and the spared {one}—by the famine, he will die. So I will complete my heat among them.
\v 13 Then you will know that I {am} Yahweh, when their slain are in the midst of their idols, all around their sacrificial altars, on every high hill—on all the tops of the mountains and under every green tree and under every leafy oak—the place where they gave there a scent of pleasing to all of their idols.
\v 14 And I will stretch out my hand against them, and I will make the land a desolation and a devastation—from the wilderness to Diblah, throughout every dwelling. And they will know that I {am} Yahweh.”’”
\f + \ft Instead of \fqa Diblah\fqa*, some ancient copies and modern versions have \fqa Riblah\fqa*.\f*
\c 7
\p
\v 1 And the word of Yahweh was to me, saying,
\v 2 “And you, son of man—thus says the Lord Yahweh to the land of Israel,
\q1 ‘End! The end has come to
\q2 the four edges of the land.
\q1 \v 3 Now, the end {is} upon you,
\q2 and I am sending my nose on you,
\q1 and I will judge you according to your ways,
\q2 and I will place on you all of your abominations.
\q1 \v 4 And my eyes will not pity you,
\q2 and I will not spare {you}.
\q1 Certainly, I will place your ways on you,
\q2 and your abominations will be in your midst.
\q2 Then you will know that I {am} Yahweh.’
\b
\q1 \v 5 Thus says the Lord Yahweh,
\q1 ‘Disaster after disaster!
\q2 Behold! It is coming.
\q1 \f + \ft Instead of \fqa Disaster! A unique disaster!\fqa* some ancient copies have \fqa Disaster after disaster\f*
\v 6 An end comes!
\q2 The end comes!
\q1 It has awoken against you.
\q2 Behold! It is coming!
\q1 \v 7 Doom is coming to you,
\q2 the ones dwelling {in} the land.
\q1 The time has come! The day {is} near—
\q2 panic and not shouts {on the} mountains.
\q1 \v 8 Now, from near, I will pour my heat against you,
\q2 and I will complete my nose on you.
\q1 And I will judge you according to your ways,
\q2 and I will place on you all your abominations.
\q1 \v 9 And my eyes will not pity,
\q2 and I will not spare.
\q1 According to your ways, I will place on you,
\q2 and your abominations will be in your midst.
\q2 Then you will know that I {am} Yahweh—{the one} smiting!
\b
\q1 \v 10 Behold! The day!
\q2 Behold! It is coming!
\q1 Doom has gone out!
\q2 The rod has blossomed;
\q2 arrogance has budded!
\q1 \v 11 Violence has gone up
\q2 into a rod of wickedness.
\q1 None {will be} of them—
\q2 and none of their crowd,
\q1 and none of their wealth,
\q2 and no prominence of theirs!
\q1 \v 12 The time is coming;
\q2 the day has struck!
\q1 Let not the buyer rejoice,
\q2 and let not the seller mourn,
\q2 for wrath {is} toward her whole crowd!
\q1 \v 13 For the seller—to the sale, he will not return
\q2 while they are yet alive,
\q1 because {the} vision regarding the whole crowd will not return;
\q2 and each one, in his iniquity, will not grasp his life.
\b
\q1 \v 14 They have blown the trumpet,
\q2 and they have established everything,
\q1 but there is no one going to war,
\q2 for my wrath {is} toward her whole crowd.
\q1 \v 15 The sword {is} outside,
\q2 and the plague and the famine—from the house.
\q1 The one in the field—by the sword, he will die;
\q2 and the one in the city—famine and plague will consume him.
\q1 \v 16 But their survivors will escape,
\q2 and they will be toward the mountains.
\q1 Like doves of the valleys, all of them will moan—
\q2 each {one} in his iniquity.
\q1 \v 17 All the hands will sink,
\q2 and all knees will go {with} water.
\q1 \v 18 And they will wear sackcloth,
\q2 and horror will cover them;
\q1 and to every face—shame,
\q2 and on all of their heads—baldness!
\b
\q1 \v 19 Their silver they will throw outside,
\q2 and their gold will be like menstruation.
\q1 Their silver and their gold
\q2 will not be able to rescue them
\q2 on the day of the rage of Yahweh.
\q1 Their throats will not be satiated,
\q2 and their bellies will not be filled,
\q2 because {it} is an obstacle of their iniquity.
\q1 \v 20 And the beauty of his jewelry—he set it as pride,
\q2 and the images of their abominations,
\q1 their abhorrences, they made with it.
\q2 Therefore, I have put {it} to them as menstruation.
\q1 \v 21 Then I will give {it} into the hand of foreigners as plunder
\q2 and to the wicked of the earth as spoil,
\q2 and they will defile it.
\q1 \v 22 And I will turn my face from them,
\q2 and they will defile my treasured {place}.
\q1 And violent {people} will enter into it,
\q2 and they will defile it.
\b
\q1 \v 23 Make a chain,
\q2 for the land {is} full of {the} judgment of blood,
\q2 and the city {is} full of violence.
\q1 \v 24 So I will bring the evils of the nations,
\q2 and they will inherit their houses,
\q1 and I will cease the pride of the mighty,
\q2 and their sanctuaries will be defiled.
\q1 \v 25 Terror is coming!
\q2 Then they will seek peace,
\q2 but none will be!
\q1 \v 26 Disaster on disaster will come,
\q1 and rumor to rumor will be.
\q1 Then they will seek a vision from a prophet,
\q2 but the instruction will perish from a priest,
\q2 and the counsel from elders.
\q1 \v 27 The king will mourn,
\q2 and the prince will wear desolation,
\q1 and the hands of the people of the land will be terrified.
\q2 From their ways, I will do to them,
\q1 and by their judgments, I will judge them.
\q2 And they will know that I am Yahweh.’”
\c 8
\p
\v 1 And it was, in the sixth year, in the sixth {month}, on the fifth of the month, I was sitting in my house, and the elders of Judah were sitting to my face. And the hand of the Lord Yahweh fell on me there.
\v 2 And I looked, and behold!—a likeness like the appearance of fire. From the appearance of his waist and downward {was} fire, and from his waist and upward {was} like the appearance of brightness, like the eye of the metal.
\v 3 And he sent out the form of a hand, and he took me by a lock of my head. Then a wind lifted me between the earth and between the heavens, and it brought me to Jerusalem in visions of God, to the entrance of the gate of the inner {court}, the one opening northward, where there {was} the seat of the image of jealousy, the one provoking jealousy.
\v 4 And behold! There {was} the glory of the God of Israel, like the appearance that I saw in the valley.
\v 5 Then he said to me, “Son of man, now lift your eyes {to} the way of the north.” So I lifted my eyes {to} the way of the north, and behold!—from the north of the gate of the altar {was} this image of jealousy at the entrance.
\b
\p
\v 6 Then he said to me, “Son of man, are you seeing what they are doing, the great abominations that the house of Israel is doing here, to make {me} far from upon my sanctuary? But you will yet return; you will see great abominations.”
\b
\p
\v 7 Then he brought me to the entrance of the courtyard. And I looked, and behold!—one hole in the wall.
\v 8 And he said to me, “Son of man, now dig into the wall.” So I dug into the wall, and behold!—one entrance.
\p
\v 9 Then he said to me, “Enter, and see the evil abominations that they are doing here.”
\v 10 So I entered, and I looked, and behold!—every form of crawling thing and detestable animal and all of the idols of the house of Israel, carved on the wall all around, all around.
\p
\v 11 And seventy men from the elders of the house of Israel (and Jaazaniah son of Shaphan was standing in their midst) were standing to their faces, and each man—his censer in his hand. And the smell of the cloud of incense was ascending.
\p
\v 12 Then he said to me, “Are you seeing, son of man, that which the elders of the house of Israel are doing in the dark—each man in the chambers of his picture? For they are saying, ‘Yahweh is not seeing us; Yahweh has abandoned the land.’”
\v 13 And he said to me, “You will yet return; you will see {the} great abominations that they are doing.”
\p
\v 14 Then he brought me to the entrance of the gate of the house of Yahweh that {was} toward the north, and behold! There, the women were sitting, weeping for the Tammuz.
\v 15 Then he said to me, “Are you seeing, son of man? Still, you will return; you will see greater abominations than these.”
\p
\v 16 So he brought me to the court of the house of Yahweh, the inner {one}, and behold! {At} the entrance of the temple of Yahweh, between the porch and between the altar—about 25 men, their backs toward the temple of Yahweh and their faces eastward, and they were prostrating themselves eastward to the sun.
\p
\v 17 Then he said to me, “Are you seeing, son of man? Is it too light for the house of Judah, doing the abominations that they have done here? For they have filled the land {with} violence, and they have returned to make me angry. And behold! They are sending the branch out to their nose!
\v 18 And so I—I will act in heat. My eye will not pity, and I will not have compassion. And they will call out in my ears {with} a great voice, but I will not hear them.”
\c 9
\p
\v 1 And he called in my ears {with} a loud voice, saying, “Draw near, executioners of the city, and each {with} the weapon of his destruction in his hand.”
\v 2 And behold! Six men were coming from the way of the upper gate that faces northward, and each {with} {the} weapon of his smashing in his hand. But one man {was} in their midst, clothed in linen, and the equipment of the scribe {was} on his waist. And they came, and they stood beside the altar of bronze.
\p
\v 3 Then the glory of the God of Israel went up from over the cherub that it had been over it, to the threshold of the house. And he called to the man, the {one} clothed in linen, whose equipment of the scribe {was} on his waist.
\v 4 Then Yahweh said to him, “Cross through the midst of the city, through the midst of Jerusalem. And you shall mark a mark on the foreheads of the men, the {ones} groaning and the {ones} sighing over all the abominations that are being done in her midst.”
\p
\v 5 And to these, he said in my ears, “Cross through the city after him and strike. Do not let your eye pity, and do not spare!
\v 6 Old {men}, young man and young woman and children and women you shall kill to destruction, but, to any man who on him {is} the mark, do not draw near. And from my sanctuary, you shall begin.” So they began with the elderly men who {were} to the face of the house.
\p
\v 7 And he said to them, “Make unclean the house, and fill the courts {with} the slain. Go out.” And they went out, and they struck in the city.
\v 8 And it was, as they struck, that I myself remained. And I fell on my face, and I cried out, and I said, “Ah, Lord Yahweh! Are you destroying the whole remnant of Israel when you pour out your heat against Jerusalem?”
\p
\v 9 Then he said to me, “The iniquity of the house of Israel and Judah is very, very great, and the land is filled {with} blood, and the city {is} full of corruption. For they say, ‘Yahweh has abandoned the land,’ and, ‘Yahweh is not seeing.’
\v 10 And so I—my eye will not pity, and I will not have compassion. Their way I have placed on their head.”
\p
\v 11 And behold! The man clothed in linen, whose equipment {was} on his waist, was returning a word, saying, “I have done just as you commanded me.”
\c 10
\p
\v 1 And I looked, and behold! To the vault that {was} over the head of the cherubim, like a stone of sapphire, {something} like the appearance of the likeness of a throne appeared over them.
\v 2 And he said to the man clothed in linen, and he said, “Go to between the wheelwork, to under the cherub, and fill your handfuls {with} coals of fire from between the cherubim, and sow {them} over the city.” And he went to my eyes.
\p
\v 3 (And the cherubim were standing from the right of the house when the man went. And the cloud filled the inner courtyard.)
\v 4 Then the glory of Yahweh arose from over the cherub to the threshold of the house. And the house was filled {with} the cloud, and the courtyard was filled {with} the brightness of the glory of Yahweh.
\v 5 And the sound of the wings of the cherubim was heard as far as the outer courtyard, like the sound of the Almighty when he speaks.
\p
\v 6 And it was, when he commanded the man clothed in linen, saying, “Take fire from between the wheelwork, from between the cherubim.” Then he went, and he stood beside the wheel.
\v 7 Then the cherub sent his hand from between the cherubim to the fire that {was} between the cherubim, and he lifted {it}, and he gave {it} to the {two} handfuls of {the one} clothed in linen. Then he took {it}, and he went out.
\v 8 (And of the cherubim was seen the form of a hand of a man under their wings.)
\p
\v 9 So I looked, and behold! Four wheels beside the cherubim, one wheel beside the one cherub, and one wheel beside the one cherub. And the appearance of the wheels {was} like the eye of a stone of topaz.
\v 10 And their appearance was one likeness for the four of them, as when the wheel is in the midst of the wheel.
\v 11 When they went, toward four of their sides they went; they did not turn when they went. For the place where the head faced, after it they went; they did not turn when they went.
\v 12 And all their flesh and their backs and their hands and their wings and the wheels {were} full of eyes all around for the four of them, their wheels.
\v 13 Of the wheels—of them was called, “The wheelwork” in my ears.
\v 14 And four of the faces {belonged} to each: The face of the first {was} the face of the cherub, and the face of the second {was} the face of a man, and the third {was} the face of a lion, and the fourth {was} the face of an eagle.
\p
\v 15 Then the cherubim arose. It {was} the beings that I saw by the river of Kebar.
\v 16 And when the cherubim went, the wheels went beside them. And when the cherubim lifted their wings to rise from over the earth—they did not turn—the wheels, also they {were} from beside them.
\v 17 When they stood, they would stand; and when they arose, they would arise {with} them, for the spirit of the beings {was} in them.
\p
\v 18 Then the glory of Yahweh went out from over the threshold of the house, and it stood over the cherubim.
\v 19 Then the cherubim lifted up their wings, and they arose from the earth to my eyes (when they went out, and the wheels {were} beside them). And it stood {at} the entrance of the gate of the house of Yahweh, the easternly {one}, and the glory of the God of Israel {was} over them from above.
\p
\v 20 (It {was} the being that I saw under the God of Israel by the river of Kebar, and I knew that they {were} cherubim.
\v 21 Four, four faces {belonged} to one, and four wings {belonged} to one, and the likeness of the hands of a man {was} under their wings.
\v 22 And the likeness of their faces—they {were} the faces that I saw along the river of Kebar, their appearances and themselves. Each went toward his faces.)
\c 11
\p
\v 1 Then a wind lifted me, and it brought me to the gate of the house of Yahweh, the easternly {one}, the {one} facing eastward, and behold! At the entrance of the gate {were} 25 men. Then I saw in their midst Jaazaniah the son of Azzur and Pelatiah the son of Benaiah, officials of the people.
\v 2 And he said to me, “Son of man, these {are} the men, the {ones} plotting iniquity and the {ones} counseling counsel of evil in this city,
\v 3 the ones saying, ‘Not near {is} building houses. She {is} the pot, but we {are} the flesh.’
\v 4 Therefore, prophesy against them! Prophesy, son of man!”
\p
\v 5 Then the Spirit of Yahweh fell on me, and he said to me, “Say, ‘Thus says Yahweh, “Thus you have said, house of Israel, and the steps of your spirit—I, I know it.
\v 6 You have multiplied your slain in this city, and you have filled her streets {with} the slain.”
\p
\v 7 Therefore, thus says the Lord Yahweh, “Your slain whom you have placed in her midst, they {are} the flesh and she {is} the pot; but you—he has brought out from her midst.
\v 8 A sword you have feared, and a sword I will bring on you”—a declaration of the Lord Yahweh.
\v 9 “So I will bring you out from her midst, and I will give you into the hand of strangers. And I will do judgments among you.
\v 10 By the sword, you will fall. On the territory of Israel, I will judge you. And you will know that I {am} Yahweh.
\v 11 She will not be for you as a pot, that you—you would be in her midst as flesh. On the territory of Israel, I will judge you,
\v 12 and you will know that I {am} Yahweh, who my statutes you have not walked and my judgments you have not done, but according to the judgments of the nations that {are} all around you, you have done.”’”
\b
\p
\v 13 And it was, when I prophesied, that Pelatiah the son of Benaiah died. So I fell on my face, and I cried out {with} a great voice, and I said, “Ah, Lord Yahweh! Are you making an end with the remnant of Israel?”
\b
\p
\v 14 Then the word of Yahweh was to me, saying,
\v 15 “Son of man, your brothers, your brothers, the men of your redemption, and all of the house of Israel, all of it, {are} those who the inhabitants of Jerusalem say of them, ‘Be far from Yahweh; to us it has been given, the land, as a property.’
\p
\v 16 Therefore say, ‘Thus says the Lord Yahweh, “Though I have made them far among the nations, and though I have dispersed them among the lands, yet I have become for them as a little sanctuary in the lands that they have come there.”’
\p
\v 17 Therefore, say, ‘Thus says the Lord Yahweh, “And I will assemble you from the peoples, and I will gather you from the lands that you have been dispersed among them. Then I will give to you the land of Israel.
\v 18 And they will come to there, and they will remove all of her detestations and all of her abominations from her.
\v 19 Then I will give to them one heart, and a new spirit I will put within you. And I will remove the heart of stone from their flesh, and I will give to them a heart of flesh,
\v 20 so that in my statutes they will walk, and my judgments they will keep and do them. And they will be to me as a people, and I—I will be to them as God.
\v 21 But, toward the heart of their detestations and their abominations, their heart is going; their way, on their head, I have put”—the declaration of the Lord Yahweh.’”
\p
\v 22 Then the cherubim lifted their wings and the wheels alongside them, and the glory of the God of Israel {was} over them from above.
\v 23 Then the glory of Yahweh ascended from over the midst of the city, and it stood over the mountain that {is} from the east of the city.
\v 24 And a wind lifted me, and it brought me to Chaldea, to the exiles, in the vision by the Spirit of God.
\b
\q1 And the vision that I had seen ascended from over me.
\v 25 And I spoke to the exiles all of the words of Yahweh that he had made me see.
\c 12
\p
\v 1 Then the word of Yahweh was to me, saying,
\v 2 “Son of man, in the midst of the house of rebellion, you are dwelling—who, eyes {belong} to them to see, but they do not see; ears {belong} to them to hear, but they do not hear, for they {are} a house of rebellion.
\p
\v 3 But you, son of man—make for yourself {the} bag of an exile, and go into exile by day to their eyes. And you shall go into exile from your place to another place to their eyes. Perhaps they will see, though they are a house of rebellion.
\v 4 And you shall bring out your bag like {the} bag of an exile by day to their eyes. But you yourself shall go out in the evening to their eyes like the going out of an exile.
\v 5 To their eyes, dig for yourself in the wall, and you shall bring {it} out through it.
\v 6 To their eyes, on a shoulder, you shall lift {it} up; in the twilight, you shall bring {it} out. Your face you shall cover so you will not see the land, for I have given you as a sign for the house of Israel.”
\p
\v 7 And I did so, just as I was commanded. My bag I brought out, like {the} bag of an exile, by day, and, in the evening, I dug for myself in the wall by hand. In the twilight, I brought {it} out; on a shoulder, I lifted {it} up to their eyes.
\p
\v 8 Then the word of Yahweh was to me in the morning, saying,
\v 9 “Son of man, has not the house of Israel, the house of rebellion, said to you, ‘What are you doing?’
\p
\v 10 Say to them, ‘Thus says the Lord Yahweh, “The prince {is} this burden in Jerusalem and all the house of Israel who they {are} in the midst of them.”’
\v 11 Say, ‘I {am} your sign. Just as I have done, so it will be done to them; into exile, into captivity, they will go.’
\p
\v 12 And the prince who {is} in the midst of them—to a shoulder, he will lift {it} in the twilight, and he will go out. Through the wall, they will dig to bring {him} out through it. His face he will cover, so that he will not see with the eye—he, the land.
\v 13 And I will spread my net over him, and he will be seized in my snare. And I will bring him into Babylon, the land of the Chaldeans, but her he will not see, and there he will die.
\v 14 And all who {are} all around him, his help and all his troops—I will scatter to every wind, and a sword I will empty after them.
\p
\v 15 And they will know that I {am} Yahweh, when I disperse them among the nations and scatter them among the lands.
\v 16 But I will retain from them men of a number from sword, from famine, and from plague, so that they may recount all their abominations among the nations that they have come there. And they will know that I {am} Yahweh.”
\p
\v 17 Then the word of Yahweh was to me, saying,
\v 18 “Son of man, your bread you shall eat with trembling, and your water you shall drink with shaking and with anxiety.
\v 19 And you shall say to the people of the land, ‘Thus says the Lord Yahweh to the dwellers of Jerusalem, concerning the land of Israel, “Their bread they will eat with anxiety, and their water they will drink with horror, because her land will be desolate from her fullness, from the violence of all who dwell in her.
\v 20 And the inhabited cities will be ruinous, and the land will become a desolation. And you will know that I am Yahweh.”’”
\b
\p
\v 21 Then the word of Yahweh was to me, saying,
\v 22 “Son of man, what {is} this proverb of yours concerning the land of Israel, saying, ‘The days lengthen, and every vision passes’?
\v 23 Therefore, say to them, ‘Thus says the Lord Yahweh, “I am ceasing this proverb, and they will not recite it anymore in Israel.”’ Except, speak to them, ‘The days are drawing near, and the word of every vision.
\v 24 For there will no longer be any vision of falsehood or divination of flattering in the midst of the house of Israel.
\v 25 For I, Yahweh—I will speak; the word that I will speak, then it will be done. It will not be delayed any longer, for in your days, house of rebellion, I will speak a word, and I will do it—the declaration of the Lord Yahweh.’”
\b
\p
\v 26 Then the word of Yahweh was to me, saying,
\v 27 “Son of man, behold! The house of Israel is saying, ‘The vision that he is envisioning {is} for many days, and for distant times he is prophesying.’
\p
\v 28 Therefore, say to them, ‘Thus says the Lord Yahweh, “All of my words will not be delayed any longer; the word that I speak, then it will be done”—the declaration of the Lord Yahweh.’”
\c 13
\p
\v 1 Then the word of Yahweh was to me, saying,
\v 2 “Son of man, prophesy to the prophets of Israel, the {ones} prophesying, and you shall say to the prophets from their heart, ‘Hear the word of Yahweh!
\v 3 Thus says the Lord Yahweh, “Woe to the foolish prophets, who are walking after their spirit but without seeing!
\v 4 Like jackals in the ruins, your prophets have become, Israel.
\v 5 You have not gone up into the breaches, nor have you built a wall for the house of Israel, to stand in the battle on the day of Yahweh.
\v 6 They have envisioned falsehood and a divination of a lie, the {ones} saying, ‘The declaration of Yahweh,’ but Yahweh—he has not sent them, and they have hoped to confirm {the} word.
\v 7 Have you not envisioned a vision of falsehood and spoken a divination of a lie, and you are saying, ‘The declaration of Yahweh,’ though I, I have not spoken?”
\p
\v 8 Therefore, thus says the Lord Yahweh, “Because you have spoken falsehood and have envisioned a lie, therefore, look at me, against you”—the declaration of the Lord Yahweh.
\v 9 “And my hand will be toward the prophets, the {ones} envisioning falsehood and the {ones} divining a lie:
\q1 In the council of my people,
\q2 they will not be,
\q1 and in the writing of the house of Israel,
\q2 they will not be written,
\q1 and to the land of Israel,
\q2 they will not come.
\q2 Then you will know that I {am} the Lord Yahweh.
\b
\p
\v 10 Because, and because, they have led my people astray, saying, ‘Peace!’ but there is no peace, and he is building a mortarless wall, and look at them!—smearing it {with} plaster.
\v 11 Say to the {ones} smearing {with} plaster, and it will fall! There will be a gushing rain, and you, stones of hailstone—you will fall, and a wind of storms will break forth.
\v 12 And behold! The wall falls. Will it not be said to you, ‘Where is the coating that you smeared?’”
\p
\v 13 Therefore, thus says the Lord Yahweh, “So I will break out a wind of storms in my heat, and a gushing rain in my nose will be, and stones of hailstones in heat, to completion.
\v 14 And I will tear down the wall that you smeared {with} plaster, and I will make it touch to the ground, and its base will be uncovered. And it will fall, and you will end in the midst of it. Then you will know that I {am} Yahweh.
\v 15 And I will end my heat on the wall and on the ones smearing it {with} plaster, and I will say to you, ‘There is no wall, and there are none smearing it—
\v 16 the prophets of Israel, the {ones} prophesying to Jerusalem and the {ones} envisioning for her a vision of peace, but there is no peace’—the declaration of the Lord Yahweh.”’
\p
\v 17 But you, son of man—set your face to the daughters of your people, the {ones} prophesying from their own heart, and prophesy against them.
\v 18 And you shall say, ‘Thus says the Lord Yahweh, “Woe to the {ones} sewing bands on all the joints of my {two} hands, and the {ones} making the amulets over the head of every height to hunt lives! Will you hunt the lives of my people but keep alive the lives of yourselves?
\v 19 And you have profaned me among my people for handfuls of barley and for crumbs of bread, to kill lives that should not die and to keep alive lives that should not live, by your lying to my people, the {ones} hearing {the} lie.”
\p
\v 20 Therefore, thus says the Lord Yahweh, “Look at me!—against your bands with which you are hunting there the lives like flying {ones}, and I will tear them from upon your arms, and I will send out the lives that you are hunting—the lives, like flying {ones}.
\v 21 And I will tear off your amulets, and I will rescue my people from your hand, and they will no longer be in your hand as prey. Then you will know that I {am} Yahweh.
\v 22 Because of disheartening the heart of a righteous {person with} falsehood—but I, I have not pained him—and strengthening the hands of a wicked {person} without turning from his evil way, to keep him alive,
\v 23 therefore, you will no longer envision falsehood, and you will no longer divine a divination! And I will rescue my people from your hand, and you will know that I {am} Yahweh.”’”
\c 14
\p
\v 1 And men from the elders of Israel came to me, and they sat to my face.
\v 2 Then the word of Yahweh was to me, saying,
\v 3 “Son of man, these men have brought up their idols on their heart, and the obstacle of their iniquity they have put opposite their faces. Being sought, will I be sought by them?
\v 4 Therefore, speak to them, and you shall say to them, ‘Thus says the Lord Yahweh, “A man, a man from the house of Israel who brings up his idols to his heart and places the obstacle of his iniquity opposite his face, and then comes to the prophet—I, Yahweh, I will answer him with it, in the multitude of his idols,
\v 5 in order to seize the house of Israel by their heart, who have become estranged from me by their idols—all of them.”’
\p
\v 6 Therefore, say to the house of Israel, ‘Thus says the Lord Yahweh, “Return! And turn away from your idols, and, from all your abominations, turn your faces!
\v 7 For a man, a man from the house of Israel, or from the sojourner who sojourns in Israel, and he consecrates himself from after me, and he brings up his idols to his heart, and he places the obstacle of his iniquity opposite his face, and then he comes to the prophet to inquire through him of me—I, Yahweh, I will answer through him of me.
\v 8 Then I will set my face against that man, and I will make him into a sign and into proverbs, and I will cut him off from the midst of my people. Then you will know that I {am} Yahweh.
\p
\v 9 And the prophet, if he is deceived and speaks a word, I, Yahweh, have deceived that prophet, and I will stretch out my hand against him, and I will destroy him from the midst of my people Israel.
\v 10 And they will carry their iniquity—the iniquity of the {one} inquiring will be like the iniquity of the prophet,
\v 11 so that the house of Israel will no longer wander away from after me, and they will no longer make themselves unclean with all their rebellions. And they will belong to me as a people, and I, I will belong to them as God”—the declaration of the Lord Yahweh.’”
\p
\v 12 Then the word of Yahweh was to me, saying,
\v 13 “Son of man, a land, if it sinned against me by violating a violation, and I stretched out my hand against it, and I broke for it a staff of bread, and I sent famine against it, and I cut off from it man and animal,
\v 14 and three of these men were in its midst—Noah, Daniel, and Job—themselves, by their righteousness, they would rescue their lives—the declaration of the Lord Yahweh.
\p
\v 15 If I made an evil creature pass through the land, and it bereaves, and it becomes a desolation, without passing through from the face of the creature,
\v 16 {and} three of these men {were} in its midst—the life of me, the declaration of the Lord Yahweh—neither sons nor daughters would they rescue; they by themselves—they would be rescued, but the land would become a desolation.
\p
\v 17 Or {if} I brought a sword against that land, and I said, ‘Let a sword pass through the land,’ and I cut off from it man and animal,
\v 18 {and} three of these men {were} in its midst—the life of me, the declaration of the Lord Yahweh—they would not rescue sons or daughters, for they by themselves, they would be rescued.
\p
\v 19 Or {if} I sent a plague to that land, and I poured out my heat against it in blood, to cut off from it man and animal,
\v 20 and Noah, Daniel, and Job {were} in its midst—the life of me, the declaration of the Lord Yahweh—neither son nor daughter would they rescue; they, by their righteousness, they would rescue their lives.
\p
\v 21 For thus says the Lord Yahweh, ‘How much more when I send my four disastrous judgments—a sword and a famine and a disastrous creature and a plague—to Jerusalem, to cut off from her man and animal!
\v 22 But behold! Survivors will be left in her, those being brought out, sons and daughters. Look at them!—going out to you, and you will see their way and their deeds, and you will be comforted concerning the disaster that I brought on Jerusalem, everything that I brought on her.
\v 23 And they will comfort you when you see their way and their deeds, and you will know that not without cause have I done all that I have done in her’—the declaration of the Lord Yahweh.”
\c 15
\p
\v 1 Then the word of Yahweh was to me, saying,
\v 2 “Son of man, what will be of the wood of the vine from every tree, of the branch that was among the trees of the forest?
\v 3 Is wood be taken from it to make for work? Or do they take from it a peg to hang on it any vessel?
\v 4 Behold! To the fire it is given as food. Two of its ends the fire consumes, and its middle is burned. Will it succeed for work?
\v 5 Behold! When it was whole, it was not made for work. How much more so when the fire has consumed it and it is burned? Will it still be made for work?
\p
\v 6 Therefore, thus says the Lord Yahweh, ‘Just like the wood of the vine among the trees of the forest, which I have given it to the fire as food, so I have given the dwellers of Jerusalem.
\v 7 So I will put my face against them. From the fire, they went out, but the fire will consume them. Then you will know that I {am} Yahweh, when I set my face against them.
\v 8 And I will make the land a desolation, because they violated a violation’—the declaration of the Lord Yahweh.”
\c 16
\p
\v 1 Then the word of Yahweh was to me, saying,
\v 2 “Son of man, make Jerusalem know her abominations,
\v 3 and you shall say, ‘Thus says the Lord Yahweh to Jerusalem, “Your origins and your birth {are} from the land of the Canaanites; your father was the Amorite, and your mother was a Hittite.
\v 4 And your birth—on the day of your being born, your navel {cord} was not cut, and with water you were not washed for cleansing. And, being salted, you were not salted, and, being swathed, you were not swathed.
\v 5 An eye did not have pity on you, to do for you one of these things, to have compassion on you; but you were thrown to the face of the field with the disdain of your life, on the day of your being born.
\p
\v 6 Then I passed by you, and I saw you kicking about in your blood. So I said to you in your blood, ‘Live!’ And I said to you in your blood, ‘Live!’
\v 7 Ten thousand, like a sprout of the field, I made you, and you multiplied, and you grew up, and you came to the jewelry of jewelry. Your breasts were established, and your hair sprouted, but you {were} naked and bare.
\p
\v 8 Then I passed by you, and I saw you, and behold!—your time {was} the time of lovers. So I spread my wing over you, and I covered your nakedness; and I swore to you, and I entered into a covenant with you”—the declaration of the Lord Yahweh—“and you became mine.
\v 9 Then I washed you with the water, and I rinsed your blood from on you, and I anointed you with oil.
\v 10 And I clothed you {with} embroidery and fastened you {with} leather, and I wrapped you {with} linen, and I covered you {with} silk.
\v 11 And I bejeweled you {with} jewelry, and I placed bracelets on your hands and a chain on your neck.
\v 12 And I placed a ring on your nose and earrings on your ears and a crown of beauty on your head.
\v 13 And you were bejeweled {with} gold and silver, and your clothing {was} linen and silk and embroidery. Flour and honey and oil you ate, and you became beautiful—very, very!—and you prospered to royalty.
\v 14 And a name went out for you among the nations of your beauty, for it {was} complete by my majesty that I had put on you”—the declaration of the Lord Yahweh.
\p
\v 15 “But you trusted in your beauty, so you prostituted yourself on account of your name. And you poured out your prostitutions onto everyone passing by—and of him it would become.
\v 16 And you took some of your garments, and you made for yourself spotted high places, and you prostituted yourself on them. To him, you went, and of him, it became.
\v 17 And you took the ornaments of your beauty from my gold and from my silver that I gave you, and you made for yourself images of a male, and you prostituted yourself with them.
\v 18 And you took the clothing of your embroidery, and you covered them. And my oil and my incense you placed to their face.
\v 19 And my bread that I gave to you—flour and oil and honey I fed you— you placed it to their face as a scent of pleasing. And it was”—the declaration of the Lord Yahweh.
\p
\v 20 “And you took your sons and your daughters, whom you bore to me, and you sacrificed them to them to eat. Was {it} little of your prostitutions,
\v 21 that you slaughtered my sons, and you gave them by making them pass through for them?
\v 22 And with all your abominations and your prostitutions, you did not remember the days of your youth, when you were naked and bare; you were kicking about in your blood.
\p
\v 23 And it was, after all your evil—woe, woe to you!”—the declaration of the Lord Yahweh—
\v 24 “that you built yourself a mound, and you made yourself a platform in every plaza.
\v 25 At the head of every road, you built your platform, and you desecrated your beauty, and you spread your legs to everyone passing by, and you multiplied your prostitutions.
\v 26 Then you prostituted yourself to the sons of Egypt, your neighbors great of flesh, and you multiplied your prostitution to anger me.
\v 27 And behold! I stretched out my hand against you, and I reduced your portion, and I gave you to the appetite of the {ones} hating you, the daughters of the Philistines, the {ones} ashamed from your way of obscenity.
\v 28 And you prostituted yourself to the sons of Assyria without your satiation, and you prostituted yourself {with} them, and yet you were not satisfied.
\v 29 And you multiplied your prostitution toward the land of merchants, toward Chaldea; and even in this you were not satisfied.
\p
\v 30 How sick {is} your heart”—the declaration of the Lord Yahweh—“when you did all these, the deed of a woman of a brazen prostitute!
\v 31 When you built your mound at the head of every road, and your platform you made at every plaza, but you were not like the prostitute, by scorning wages.
\p
\v 32 The adulterous woman—instead of her husband, she takes strangers!
\v 33 To all prostitutes, they give a gift, but you—you gave your gifts to all your lovers, and you bribed them to come to you from all around in exchange for your prostitutions.
\v 34 And it was with you the opposite from the women in your prostitutions; and after you, one did not prostitute. So, when you gave payment, and payment was not given to you, you became the opposite.”
\p
\v 35 Therefore, prostitute, hear the word of Yahweh!
\v 36 Thus says the Lord Yahweh, “Because your passion was poured out, and your nakedness was uncovered in your prostitutions with your lovers, and because of all the idols of your abominations, and like the blood of your sons whom you gave to them,
\v 37 therefore, look {at} me!—gathering all your lovers, whom you were pleasing to them, and all whom you loved, along {with} all whom you hated. And I will gather them against you from all around, and I will uncover your nakedness to them, and they will see all your nakedness.
\v 38 And I will judge you with the judgments of adulteresses and shedders of blood, and I will make you the blood of heat and jealousy.
\v 39 So I will give you into their hand, and they will tear down your mound and break down your platforms, and they will strip you of your clothing, and they will take the vessels of your beauty, and they will leave you naked and bare.
\v 40 And they will bring up against you an assembly, and they will stone you with stones, and they will slaughter you with their swords.
\v 41 And they will burn your houses with fire, and they will do judgments against you to the eyes of many women; and I will make you cease from prostituting yourself, and also you will no longer give wages.
\v 42 And I will pacify my heat against you, and my jealousy will turn aside from you, and I will be quiet, and no longer will I be angry.
\p
\v 43 Because you did not remember the days of your youth, but you agitated me with all these, so I—behold!—I have placed your way on your head”—the declaration of the Lord Yahweh. “And have you not done this obscenity alongside all your abominations?
\p
\v 44 Behold! Everyone who uses a proverb against you—they will use a proverb, saying, ‘As the mother {is} her daughter.’
\v 45 The daughter of your mother {are} you, the one loathing her husband and her sons, and the sister of your sisters {are} you, who loathed their husbands and their sons. Your mother {was} a Hittite, and your father {was} an Amorite.
\v 46 And your sister, the greater {one, is} Samaria, she and her daughters, the one dwelling on your left; and your sister, the {one} smaller than you, the one dwelling on your right, {is} Sodom and her daughters.
\v 47 And in their ways did you not walk, and according to their abominations did you {not} act? In very little {time}, so you were corrupt, more than them, in all your ways.
\v 48 The life of me”—the declaration of the Lord Yahweh—“if Sodom your sister, she and her daughters, did just as you have done—you and your daughters!
\p
\v 49 Behold! This was the iniquity of Sodom, your sister: Pride, abundance of bread, and quiet ease belonged to her and to her daughters, but the hand of the poor and needy she did not strengthen.
\v 50 And they were haughty, and they did an abomination to my face, so I removed them, just as I saw.
\v 51 And Samaria—as half of your sins she did not sin, but you multiplied your abominations more than they, and you made your sister righteous by all your abominations that you did.
\v 52 Also you—carry your humiliation that you have adjudged for your sister. In your sins—{in} which you acted more abominably than they—they are more righteous than you. So you also, be ashamed and carry your humiliation of your making your sisters righteous.
\p
\v 53 And I will restore their fortune—the fortune of Sodom and her daughters, and the fortune of Samaria and her daughters—and the fortunes of your fortunes in their midst,
\v 54 so that you may carry your humiliation and be humiliated because of all that you did, when you comforted them.
\v 55 And your sisters, Sodom and her daughters—they will return to their former state; and Samaria and her daughters—they will return to their former state; and you and your daughters—you will return to your former state.
\v 56 And did not Sodom your sister become a report in your mouth in the day of your pride,
\v 57 before your evil was uncovered? Like her, you {are} the reproach of the daughters of Aram and all {those} all around her, the daughters of the Philistines, the ones despising you from all around.
\v 58 Your obscenity and your abominations, you yourself have carried them”—the declaration of Yahweh.
\p
\v 59 For thus says the Lord Yahweh, “So I will do to you just as you have done, when you despised an oath by breaking a covenant.
\v 60 But I myself will remember my covenant with you in the days of your youth, and I will establish for you an everlasting covenant.
\v 61 Then you will remember your ways, and you will be humiliated when you take your sisters, the {ones} greater than you, along with the {ones} smaller than you; and I will give them to you as daughters, but not from your covenant.
\v 62 And I myself will establish my covenant with you, and you will know that I {am} Yahweh,
\v 63 so that you may remember and you may be ashamed, and no longer will an opening of the mouth be for you from the face of your humiliation, when I make atonement for you for all that you have done”—the declaration of the Lord Yahweh.’”
\c 17
\p
\v 1 Then the word of Yahweh was to me, saying,
\v 2 “Son of man, propose a riddle and speak a parable to the house of Israel.
\v 3 And you shall say, ‘Thus says the Lord Yahweh,
\q1 “The great eagle, great of wings,
\q1 long of the feather, full of plumage,
\q1 which {belonged} to him the embroidery,
\q1 came to Lebanon, and he took the top of the cedar.
\q1 \v 4 The head of its shoots he plucked,
\q1 and he brought it to the land of Canaan;
\q1 in a city of traders he put it.
\b
\q1 \v 5 And he took from the seed of the land,
\q1 and he put it in a field of seed,
\q1 a meadow along many waters;
\q1 {as} a willow he put it.
\q1 \v 6 And it sprouted,
\q1 and it became a spreading vine, low of height,
\q1 by turning its branches toward him,
\q1 and its roots were under it.
\q1 And it became as a vine, and it made poles,
\q1 and it sent out boughs.
\b
\q1 \v 7 And there was one great eagle,
\q1 great of wings and abundant of plumage.
\q1 And behold! This vine bent its roots toward him,
\q1 and it sent out its branches toward him
\q1 to water it from the beds of its planting.
\q1 \v 8 To a good field,
\q1 to many waters,
\q1 it was planted,
\q1 to make branches and to bear fruit,
\q1 to become a vine of magnificence.”’
\b
\v 9 Say, ‘Thus says the Lord Yahweh,
\q1 “Will it prosper?
\q1 Will he not tear up its roots
\q1 and will he {not} strip off its fruit,
\q1 and it will wither?
\q1 All the leaves of its sprouting will wither.
\q1 (And not with a great arm
\q1 or with many people {will be} to lift it from its roots.)
\q1 \v 10 And behold!
\q1 Planted, will it prosper?
\q1 Will it not wither when the wind of the east strikes it?
\q1 Withering, it will wither on the beds of its sprouting.”’”
\p
\v 11 Then the word of Yahweh was to me, saying,
\v 12 “Say now to the house of rebellion, ‘Do you not know what these are?’ Say, ‘Behold! The king of Babylon came {to} Jerusalem, and he took her king and her princes, and he brought them to him, to Babylon.
\v 13 And he took some of the seed of the kingdom, and he cut a covenant with him, and he caused him to enter into an oath. And the rams of the land he took
\v 14 to become a lowly kingdom, without lifting itself up, to keep his covenant for her to stand.
\v 15 But he rebelled against him by sending his messengers {to} Egypt, to give to him horses and many people. Will he prosper? Will the {one} doing these {things} escape? And he broke a covenant, but will he escape?
\p
\v 16 The life of me—the declaration of the Lord Yahweh—if not in the place of the king who made him king, who he despised his oath and who he broke his covenant, with him in the midst of Babylon, he will die.
\v 17 And not with a large army and with a great assembly, Pharaoh will act for him in the war, when a mound is poured out, and a siege wall is built, to cut off many lives.
\v 18 And he forsook an oath by breaking a covenant, and behold! He gave his hand, but he did all these {things}. He will not escape!
\p
\v 19 Therefore, thus says the Lord Yahweh, “The life of me, if not my oath that he forsook and my covenant that he broke—I will bring it on his head.
\v 20 And I will spread over him my net, and he will be caught in my snare. And I will cause him to come to Babylon, and I will litigate with him there {for} his violation that he violated against me.
\v 21 And all his refugees among all his troops will fall by the sword, and the {ones} remaining to every wind will be scattered. Then you will know that I, Yahweh, have spoken.”
\p
\v 22 Thus says the Lord Yahweh, “And I will take, I, from the top of the high cedar, and I will place {it}; from the head of its shoots, I will pluck off a tender {one}, and I will plant {it}, I, on a high and tall mountain.
\v 23 On the mountain of the height of Israel, I will plant it, and it will carry a branch, and it will make fruit, and it will become a mighty cedar. And under it will dwell every bird; every wing, in the shade of its branches, they will dwell.
\v 24 And all the trees of the field will know that I {am} Yahweh. I have brought low the high tree; I have raised high the low tree; I have withered the fresh tree, and I have made the dry tree sprout. I, Yahweh, have spoken, and I have acted.”’”
\c 18
\p
\v 1 Then the word of Yahweh was to me, saying,
\v 2 “What {is} to you, you using this proverb concerning the land of Israel, saying,
\q1 ‘Fathers eat sour grapes,
\q2 and the teeth of the sons are blunted’?
\p
\v 3 The life of me—the declaration of the Lord Yahweh—if using this proverb will yet be for you in Israel.
\v 4 Behold! All the lives—they {belong} to me; as the life of the father so as the life of the son, they {belong} to me. The life, the sinning {one}, it will die.
\p
\q1 \v 5 And a man, if he is righteous,
\q1 and he does justice and righteousness—
\q1 \v 6 on the mountains, he does not eat,
\q2 and his eyes he does not lift to the idols of the house of Israel,
\q1 and the wife of his neighbor he does not make unclean,
\q2 and to a woman of menstruation, he does not approach;
\q1 \v 7 and a man he does not oppress.
\q2 His pledge he returns {to} a debtor.
\q1 Robbery he does not rob;
\q2 his bread he gives to the hungry,
\q2 and nakedness he covers {with} clothing.
\q1 \v 8 With interest, he does not give,
\q2 and usury he does not take;
\q1 from perversity, he turns back his hand;
\q2 a judgment of truth he does between a man and a man;
\q1 \v 9 in my statutes, he walks,
\q2 and my judgments he keeps,
\q2 to do truth—
\q1 righteous {is} he.
\q2 Living, he will live—
\q2 the declaration of the Lord Yahweh.
\p
\q1 \v 10 Then he begets a violent son, {one} pouring out blood, and he does {to} a brother from one of these {things}\f + \ft Some ancient copies and versions omit \fqa to a brother\fqa*.\f*—
\v 11 But he, all of these he did not do—
\q1 for he even eats on the mountains,
\q2 and the wife of his neighbor he defiles;
\q1 \v 12 the poor and needy he oppresses;
\q2 robberies he robs;
\q1 a pledge he does not return;
\q2 and to the idols he lifts his eyes;
\q2 an abomination he does;
\q1 \v 13 with interest he gave,
\q2 and usury he took—
\q1 and will he live?
\q2 He will not live!
\q1 All these abominations he did.
\q2 Dying, he will be put to death;
\q2 his blood will be upon him.
\p
\v 14 And behold! He begets a son, and he sees all the sins of his father that he did, and he sees, and he does not do like them.
\b
\q1 \v 15 On the mountains he does not eat,
\q2 and his eyes he does not lift to the idols of the house of Israel;
\q2 the wife of his neighbor he does not defile;
\q1 \v 16 and a man he does not oppress;
\q2 a pledge he does not take in pledge,
\q1 and robbery he does not rob;
\q2 his bread to the hungry, he gives,
\q2 and the naked he covers {with} clothing;
\q1 \v 17 from perversity, he turns back his hand;
\q2 interest and usury he does not take;
\q1 my judgments he does;
\q2 in my statutes, he walks—
\q1 he, he will not die in the iniquity of his father.
\q2 Living, he will live!
\b
\v 18 His father, because he oppressed an oppression, robbed the robbery of a brother, and what {is} not good he did in the midst of his people—behold! He dies in his iniquity.
\v 19 But you say, ‘Why does the son not carry the iniquity of the father?’ And the son does justice and righteousness; all my statutes, he keeps, and he does them—living, he will live!
\v 20 The life, the {one} sinning—it will die. A son will not carry the iniquity of the father, and a father will not carry the iniquity of the son. The righteousness of the righteous will be upon him, and the wickedness of the wicked will be upon him.
\p
\v 21 But the wicked, if he turns from all his sins that he did, and he keeps all my statutes, and he does justice and righteousness—living, he will live; he will not die.
\v 22 All his rebellions that he did—they will not be remembered of him; in his righteousness that he did, he will live.
\v 23 Delighting, do I delight {in} the death of {the} wicked—the declaration of the Lord Yahweh? {Is} it not when he turns from his ways that he will live?
\v 24 But when {the} righteous turns from his righteousness and does iniquity; as all the abominations that the wicked does, he does—and shall he live? All his righteous deeds that he did—they will not be remembered; in his violation that he violated, and in his sin that he sinned—in them, he will die.
\p
\v 25 But you say, ‘The way of the Lord is not correct.’ Listen, now, house of Israel! My way—is it not correct? Is it not your ways—they are not correct?
\v 26 When {the} righteous turns from his righteousness, and he does iniquity, then he dies because of them; in his injustice that he did he dies.
\v 27 And when {the} wicked turns from his wickedness that he did, and does justice and righteousness, he, his life he will keep alive
\v 28 And {if} he sees, and he turns from all his rebellions that he did— living he will live; he will not die.
\v 29 But the house of Israel says, ‘The way of the Lord is not correct.’ My ways—are they not correct, house of Israel? Is it not your ways—they are not correct?
\v 30 Therefore, a man—according to his ways, I will judge you, house of Israel—the declaration of the Lord Yahweh. Turn and turn from all your rebellions, and it will not be for you as an obstacle of iniquity.
\v 31 Throw from upon you all your rebellions that you rebelled with them, and make for yourselves a new heart and a new spirit. And why should you die, house of Israel?
\v 32 For I do not delight in the death of the dying {one}—the declaration of the Lord Yahweh—so turn back and live!”
\c 19
\p
\v 1 “And you, take up a lament against the princes of Israel,
\v 2 and you shall say,
\q1 ‘What was your mother? A lioness!
\q1 Between lions,
\q2 she crouched;
\q1 in the midst of young lions,
\q2 she increased her cubs.
\q1 \v 3 And she raised up one from her cubs; he became a young lion,
\q2 and he learned to tear prey;
\q2 he ate men.
\q1 \v 4 And the nations heard about him;
\q2 in their pit, he was caught,
\q1 and they brought him with hooks
\q2 to the land of Egypt.
\q1 \v 5 And she saw that she had hoped,
\q2 that her hope had perished,
\q1 and she took one of her cubs;
\q2 she appointed him a young lion.
\q1 \v 6 And he walked about in the midst of lions;
\q2 he became a young lion,
\q1 and he learned to tear prey;
\q2 he ate men.
\q1 \v 7 And he knew his widows,
\q2 and he laid waste their cities,
\q1 and the land and its fullness were desolate
\q2 from the sound of his roaring.
\q1 \f + \ft Instead of \fqa And he knew his widows\fqa*, some ancient copies and many modern versions have \fqa And he destroyed their fortresses\fqa*.\f*
\v 8 But they put against him—
\q2 {the} nations all around, from the provinces—
\q1 and they spread over him their net;
\q2 in their pit, he was caught.
\q1 \v 9 And they put him in the cage with hooks,
\q2 and they brought him to the king of Babylon;
\q1 they brought him into the strongholds
\q2 so that his voice would not be heard anymore
\q2 on the mountains of Israel.
\q1 \v 10 Your mother {was} like a vine in your blood;
\q2 beside the waters, she was planted.
\q1 Fruitful\f + \ft Instead of \fqa in your blood\fqa*, some ancient copies and many modern versions have \fqa in your vineyard\fqa*.\f* and full of branches was she,
\q2 from many waters.
\q1 \v 11 And belonged to her rods of strength,
\q2 toward the scepters of rulers,
\q1 and her height grew tall,
\q2 upon among the clouds,
\q1 and it was seen in its height,
\q2 in {the} abundance of its branches.
\q1 \v 12 But she was uprooted in heat;
\q2 she was thrown to the ground,
\q1 and a wind of the east withered her fruit.
\q2 They were stripped,
\q1 and they withered, the rod of her strength,
\q2 and fire consumed it.
\q1 \v 13 So now, she is planted in the wilderness,
\q2 in a land of drought and thirst.
\q1 \v 14 And fire went out from a rod of her shoots;
\q2 it consumed her fruit,
\q1 and within her was not a rod of strength—
\q2 no scepter to rule.’
\p It {is} a lament, and it has become as a lament.”
\c 20
\p
\v 1 And it was, in the seventh year, in the fifth {month}, on the tenth of the month, men from the elders of Israel came to seek Yahweh, and they sat to my face.
\v 2 Then the word of Yahweh was to me, saying,
\v 3 “Son of man, speak {to} the elders of Israel, and you shall say to them, ‘Thus says the Lord Yahweh, “Is it to ask me {that} you are coming? The life of me, if I will be asked by you”—the declaration of the Lord Yahweh.’
\p
\v 4 Will you judge them? Will you judge, son of man? Make them know the abominations of their fathers!
\v 5 And you shall say to them, ‘Thus says the Lord Yahweh, “On the day of my choosing of Israel, and I lifted my hand to the seed of the house of Jacob, and I made myself known to them in the land of Egypt. And I lifted my hand to them, saying. ‘I {am} Yahweh, your God!’
\v 6 On that day, I lifted my hand to them, to bring them out from the land of Egypt to a land that I had searched out for them, flowing with milk and honey; it {was} beauty to all the lands.
\v 7 And I said to them, ‘A man—the detestations of his eye, throw away, and with the idols of Egypt, do not make yourself unclean. I {am} Yahweh, your God!’
\v 8 But they rebelled against me, and they were not willing to listen to me. Each man—the detestations of his eyes they did not throw away, and the idols of Egypt they did not forsake. So I said to pour my heat on them, to complete my nose against them in the midst of the land of Egypt.
\v 9 But I acted for the sake of my name, without being profaned to the eyes of the nations, which they {were} in the midst of them, which I made myself known to them, to their eyes, by bringing them out from the land of Egypt.
\p
\v 10 So I brought them out from the land of Egypt, and I brought them to the wilderness.
\v 11 And I gave to them my statutes, and my judgments I made known {to} them. The man who does them, so he will live by them.
\v 12 And also my Sabbaths I gave to them, to be as a sign between me and between them, to know that I {am} Yahweh, the {one} sanctifying them.
\v 13 But the house of Israel rebelled against me in the wilderness. In my statutes, they did not walk, and my judgments they rejected, which the man who does them, then he will live by them; and my Sabbaths they profaned exceedingly. So I said to pour out my heat on them in the wilderness, to finish them.
\v 14 But I acted for the sake of my name, without being profaned to the eyes of the nations, who I brought them out to their eyes.
\v 15 And also I, I lifted my hand to them in the wilderness, without bringing them into the land that I had given, flowing with milk and honey— a beauty it {is} for all the lands—
\v 16 because my judgments they rejected, and my statutes—they did not walk in them, and my Sabbaths they profaned; for after their idols, their heart was walking.
\v 17 But my eye had pity on them, from destroying them, and I did not make them a complete end in the wilderness.
\p
\v 18 And I said to their sons in the wilderness, ‘In the statutes of your fathers, do not walk, and their judgments do not keep, and, with their idols, do not make yourselves unclean.
\v 19 I {am} Yahweh your God. In my statutes, walk, and my judgments keep and do them.
\v 20 And my Sabbaths make holy, and they will be as a sign between me and between you, to know that I {am} Yahweh your God.’
\v 21 But the sons rebelled against me. In my statutes, they did not walk, and my judgments they did not keep, to do them—the man who does them, so he will live by them; my Sabbaths they profaned. So I said to pour out my heat on them, to complete my nose against them in the wilderness.
\v 22 But I returned my hand, and I acted for the sake of my name, without being profaned to the eyes of the nations, who I had brought them out to their eyes.
\v 23 Also I, I lifted my hand to them in the wilderness, to scatter them among the nations and to disperse them among the lands,
\v 24 because my judgments they did not do, and my statutes they rejected, and my Sabbaths they profaned, and after the idols of their fathers, their eyes were.
\v 25 And also I, I gave to them statutes not good, and judgments {that} they could not live by them.
\v 26 And I made them unclean by their gifts, in making every firstborn of the womb to pass, so that I might desolate them, so that they would know that I {am} Yahweh.”’
\v 27 Therefore speak to the house of Israel, son of man, and you shall say to them, ‘Thus says the Lord Yahweh, “Still this, your fathers blasphemed me, when they violated a violation against me.
\v 28 And I brought them into the land that I lifted my hand to give it to them, and they saw every high hill and every leafy tree, and they sacrificed there their sacrifices, and they gave there the anger of their offering, and they placed there the aroma of their pleasing {offering}, and they poured out there their drink offerings.
\v 29 And I said to them, ‘What {is} the high place that you {are} the going one there?’” And its name was called Bamah until this day.’
\p
\v 30 Therefore, say to the house of Israel, ‘Thus says the Lord Yahweh, “In the way of your fathers, are you making yourselves unclean, and after their detestations, are you prostituting yourselves?
\v 31 And when you lifted your gifts, when you made your sons to pass through the fire, you are making yourselves unclean by all your idols until today. And I, shall I be sought by you, house of Israel? The life of me”—the declaration of the Lord Yahweh—“if I will be sought by you.
\v 32 And the {thing} ascending on your spirit—being, it will not be—that you are saying, ‘We will be like the nations, like the clans of the lands, to serve wood and stone.’
\p
\v 33 The life of me”—the declaration of the Lord Yahweh—“if not, with a strong hand and with an outstretched arm and with heat poured out, I will reign over you.
\v 34 And I will bring you out from the peoples, and I will gather you from the lands that you were scattered in them, with a strong hand and with an outstretched arm and with wrath poured out.
\v 35 And I will bring you to the wilderness of the peoples, and I will litigate with you there, face to face.
\v 36 Just as I litigated with your fathers in the wilderness of the land of Egypt, so I will litigate with you”—the declaration of the Lord Yahweh.
\v 37 “And I will make you pass under the rod, and I will bring you into the bond of the covenant.
\v 38 And I will purge from you the rebels and the {ones} transgressing against me. From the land of their sojournings, I will bring them out, but to the land of Israel, he will not come. Then you will know that I {am} Yahweh.”
\v 39 And you, house of Israel, thus says the Lord Yahweh, “Each man, his idols—go, serve; and afterward, if you are not listening to me. But the name of my holiness you will not profane any longer with your gifts and with your idols.
\p
\v 40 For on the mountain of my holiness, on the mountain of the height of Israel”—the declaration of the Lord Yahweh—“there, all the house of Israel, all of it, will serve me in the land. There, I will accept them, and there I will seek your contributions and the first of your tributes, with all your holy {offerings}.
\v 41 With an aroma of pleasing, I will accept you, when I bring you out from the peoples, and I gather you from the lands that you were scattered in them, then I will be sanctified among you to the eyes of the nations.
\v 42 Then you will know that I {am} Yahweh, when I bring you to the land of Israel, to the land that I lifted my hand to give it to your fathers.
\v 43 And there, you will remember your ways and all your deeds that you defiled yourselves with them, and you will loathe yourselves in your faces by all your evils that you did.
\v 44 And you will know that I am Yahweh, when I act with you for the sake of my name, not according to your evil ways or according to your ruined deeds, house of Israel”— the declaration of the Lord Yahweh.’”
\p
\v 45 Then the word of Yahweh was to me, saying,
\v 46 “Son of man, set your face {to} the way, to Teman, and drivel to Darom, and prophesy to the forest of the field of the Negev.
\v 47 And you shall say to the forest of the Negev, ‘Hear the word of Yahweh! Thus says the Lord Yahweh: “Look at me—kindling in you a fire, and it will eat in you every fresh tree and every dry tree. The flame of the blaze will not be quenched, and all faces from the south to the north will be scorched by it.
\v 48 And all flesh will see that I, Yahweh, have burned it. It will not be quenched.”’”
\v 49 And I said, “Ah, Lord Yahweh! They are saying to me, ‘Is he not a user of proverbs?’”
\c 21
\p
\v 1 Then the word of Yahweh was to me, saying,
\v 2 “Son of man, set your face toward Jerusalem, and drivel against the sanctuaries, and prophesy against the land of Israel.
\v 3 And you shall say to the land of Israel, ‘Thus says Yahweh, “Look at me—against you! And I will bring out my sword from its sheath, and I will cut off from you righteous and wicked.
\v 4 Because I cut off from you righteous and wicked, therefore my sword will go out from its sheath against all flesh from the south {to} the north.
\v 5 And all flesh will know that I, Yahweh, have brought out my sword from its sheath. It will not return again.’”
\p
\v 6 And you, son of man, groan with {the} breaking of loins, and, with bitterness, you shall groan to their eyes.
\v 7 And it will be that they will say to you, ‘On account of what are you groaning?’ Then you shall say, ‘Because of a report, for it is coming. And every heart will melt, and all hands will slacken, and every spirit will dim, and all knees will go {with} water. Behold! It is coming, and it will happen—the declaration of the Lord Yahweh.’”
\p
\v 8 And the word of Yahweh was to me, saying,
\v 9 “Son of man, prophesy and say, ‘Thus says the Lord.’ Say,
\q1 ‘A sword, a sword,
\q2 sharpened and also polished—
\q1 \v 10 For the sake of slaughtering a slaughter, it has been sharpened;
\q2 for the sake of belonging to it lightning, it has been polished.
\q2 Or shall we rejoice? The scepter of my son is despising every tree.
\q1 \v 11 And he gave it to polish,
\q2 to seize {it} in the palm.
\q1 It has been sharpened, the sword;
\q2 and it, it has been polished,
\q2 to give it into the hand of a killer.
\q1 \v 12 Cry out and wail, son of man,
\q2 for it is against my people;
\q2 it is against all the leaders of Israel.
\q1 {The ones} thrown to the sword, they are, with my people!
\q2 Therefore, slap on the thigh!
\q1 \v 13 For it has been tested.
\q2 And what if even the rejecting scepter will not be?—the declaration of the Lord Yahweh.’
\b
\q1 \v 14 And you, son of man, prophesy,
\q2 and strike palm to palm,
\q1 and may the sword be doubled—
\q2 three {times}!
\q1 It {is} the sword of the slain;
\q2 it {is} the sword of the great slain one,
\q2 the {one} enclosing them,
\q1 \v 15 for the sake of the melting of {the} heart
\q2 and the multiplying of the obstacles.
\q1 On all their gates,
\q2 I have put the point of a sword.
\q1 Ah! It is made for lightning;
\q2 it is withdrawn for slaughter.
\q1 \v 16 Gather yourself! Go to the right!
\q2 Set yourself! Go to the left!
\q2 Wherever your face is appointed!
\q1 \v 17 And also I—I will strike my palm to my palm,
\q2 and I will settle my heat.
\q2 I, Yahweh, have spoken.”
\p
\v 18 Then the word of Yahweh was to me, saying,
\v 19 “And you, son of man, set for yourself two ways for the sword of the king of Babylon to come; from one land the two of them will go out. And create a hand; at the head of the way to a city create {it}.
\v 20 A way you shall set for the sword to come to Rabbah of the sons of Ammon, and to Judah, in fortified Jerusalem.
\v 21 For the king of Babylon stands at the mother of the way, at the head of the two ways, to divine a divination. He shakes the arrows; he inquires of the idols; he looks at the liver.
\v 22 On his right is the divination {for} Jerusalem, to set battering rams, to open the mouth with murder, to lift up the voice with a shout, to set battering rams against the gates, to pour out a siege mound, to build a siege wall.
\v 23 And it will be to them like a divination of emptiness in their eyes. Sworn oaths {belong} to them, but he is reminding of iniquity to be captured.
\p
\v 24 Therefore, thus says the Lord Yahweh: ‘Because of remembering your iniquity, in the uncovering of your rebellions, so that your sins are seen in all your deeds—because of your being remembered, by the palm you will be seized.’
\p
\v 25 And you, profane wicked one, prince of Israel, who has come his day at the time of {the} iniquity of {the} end,
\v 26 thus says the Lord Yahweh: ‘Remove the turban and lift off the crown! This—not this! Make high the low, and make low the high.
\v 27 A ruin, a ruin, a ruin I will make it! Also this will not be, until {the one} who {belongs} to him the judgment comes, and I will give it.’
\p
\v 28 And you, son of man, prophesy, and you shall say, ‘Thus says the Lord Yahweh concerning the sons of Ammon and concerning their reproach.’ And you shall say, ‘A sword, a sword opened for slaughter, polished to consume, for the sake of lightning,
\v 29 when they envision emptiness of you, when they divine a lie of you, to put you on the necks of the profane wicked, who their day has come at the time of {the} iniquity of {the} end.
\v 30 Return to its sheath! In the place where you were created, in the land of your origins, I will judge you.
\v 31 And I will pour on you my indignation. With the fire of my wrath, I will blow against you, and I will give you into the hand of brutish men, craftsmen of destruction.
\v 32 For the fire, you will be as food. Your blood will be in the midst of the land. You will not be remembered, for I, Yahweh, have spoken.’”
\c 22
\p
\v 1 Then the word of Yahweh was to me, saying,
\v 2 “And you, son of man, will you judge? Will you judge the city of blood? And you will make her know all her abominations?
\v 3 And you shall say, ‘Thus says the Lord Yahweh: “A city pouring blood in her midst, so that her time may come—and she has made idols against herself, to become unclean.
\v 4 With your blood that you have poured, you have become guilty, and with your idols that you have made, you have become unclean. And you have brought your days near, and you have come to your years. Therefore, I have given you {as} a reproach to the nations and {as} a mockery to all the lands.
\v 5 The near {ones} and the {ones} far from you—they will mock you, unclean of the name, great of the turmoil.
\p
\v 6 Behold! The princes of Israel, each man to his arm—they are in you in order to pour blood.
\v 7 Father and mother, they have lightened in you; toward the foreigner they have acted with oppression in your midst; the fatherless and the widow they have wronged in you.
\v 8 My holy things you have despised, and my Sabbaths you have profaned.
\v 9 Men of slander, they have been in you in order to pour blood; and on the mountains, they have eaten in you; obscenity they have done in your midst.
\v 10 The nakedness of a father, he has uncovered in you; the unclean {one} of menstruation, they have abused in you.
\v 11 And a man—with the wife of his neighbor, he has done an abomination; and a man—his daughter-in-law, he has made unclean with obscenity; and a man—his sister, the daughter of his father, he has abused in you.
\v 12 A bribe they have taken in you in order to pour blood. Interest and usury you have taken, and you have gained {from} your neighbors with oppression. And me, you have forgotten”—the declaration of the Lord Yahweh.
\p
\v 13 “And behold! I have struck my palm at your gain that you have made and against your blood that is in your midst.
\v 14 Will your heart stand, or will your hands be strong, for the days that I am doing with you? I, Yahweh, have spoken, and I will do {it}.
\v 15 And I will scatter you among the nations, and I will disperse you among the lands, and I will complete your uncleanness from you.
\v 16 And you will be profaned in yourself to the eyes of the nations. And you will know that I am Yahweh.”’”
\p
\v 17 Then the word of Yahweh was to me, saying,
\v 18 “Son of man, the house of Israel has become to me as dross. All of them are bronze and tin and iron and lead in the midst of a furnace; dross of silver they have become.
\v 19 Therefore, thus says the Lord Yahweh: ‘Because all of you have become as dross, therefore, behold me, collecting you into the midst of Jerusalem.
\v 20 A collection of silver and bronze and iron and lead and tin into the midst of a furnace, to blow fire on it, to melt {it}—thus I will collect {you} in my nose and in my heat, and I will set, and I will melt you.
\v 21 And I will gather you, and I will blow on you with the fire of my wrath, and you will be melted in her midst.
\v 22 As the melting of silver in the midst of a furnace, thus you will be melted in her midst. Then you will know that I, Yahweh, have poured my heat on you.’”
\p
\v 23 Then the word of Yahweh was to me, saying,
\v 24 “Son of man, say to her, ‘You are a land—it has not been cleansed. Her rain {is} not in the day of indignation.
\v 25 A conspiracy of her prophets {is} in her midst, like a lion roaring, tearing prey. A life they have eaten; wealth and precious {things} they have taken; her widows they have multiplied in her midst.
\v 26 Her priests have done violence to my law, and they have profaned my holy things. Between holy and common, they have not separated, and between the unclean and the clean, they have not made known, and from my Sabbaths, they have hidden their eyes. So I am profaned in their midst.
\v 27 Her princes within her {are} like wolves tearing prey, to pour blood, to destroy lives, for the sake of profiting profit.
\v 28 And her prophets have smeared for themselves {with} whitewash, envisioning emptiness and divining a lie for themselves, saying, “Thus says the Lord Yahweh,” but Yahweh has not spoken!
\v 29 The people of the land have oppressed an oppression and robbed a robbery, and the poor and the needy they have wronged, and the foreigner they have oppressed without justice.
\v 30 And I sought from them a man walling up a wall and standing in the gap to my face on behalf of the land, so that I would not destroy her; but I did not find {one}.
\v 31 So I have poured my indignation on them; with the fire of my wrath, I have finished them. Their way on their head I have given—the declaration of the Lord Yahweh.’”
\c 23
\p
\v 1 Then the word of Yahweh was to me, saying,
\v 2 “Son of man, there were two women, daughters of one mother.
\v 3 And they prostituted in Egypt; in their youth, they prostituted. There, their breasts were squeezed, and there, they handled the nipples of their virginity.
\v 4 And their names {were} Oholah, the older, and Oholibah, her sister. And they became mine, and they bore sons and daughters. And their names: Samaria is Oholah, and Jerusalem is Oholibah.
\p
\v 5 And Oholah prostituted under me, and she lusted toward her lovers, to Assyria—fighters
\v 6 clothed {with} blue, governors and prefects, young men of desire—all of them—horsemen, riders of horses.
\v 7 And she gave her prostitutions to them, the choicest of the sons of Assyria, all of them; and with everyone whom she lusted {toward}, with all their idols, she became unclean.
\v 8 And her prostitutions from Egypt she did not forsake, for they had lain with her in her youth, and they—they handled the nipples of her virginity, and they poured their prostitution on her.
\v 9 Therefore, I gave her into the hand of her lovers, into the hand of the sons of Assyria, whom she lusted toward them.
\v 10 They, they uncovered her nakedness; her sons and her daughters they took, and her they killed with the sword. And she became a name for women, and they did judgments on her.
\p
\v 11 And her sister Oholibah saw, and she corrupted her lust more than her, and her prostitutions more than the prostitutions of her sister.
\v 12 Toward the sons of Assyria, she lusted: governors and prefects, fighters, clothed in perfection, horsemen, riders of horses, young men of desire—all of them.
\v 13 And I saw that she had become unclean; one way {belonged} to the two of them.
\v 14 And she added to her prostitutions. And she saw men carved on the wall, images of the Chaldeans engraved in vermilion,
\v 15 wearing a belt on their hips, {with} hanging turbans on their heads, the appearance of captains—all of them, the likeness of the sons of Babylon, Chaldea, the land of their birth.
\v 16 And she lusted toward them by the sight of her eyes, and she sent messengers to them, to Chaldea.
\v 17 And they came to her, the sons of Babylon, to the bed of love, and they made her unclean with their prostitution. And she became unclean by them, and her soul turned away from them.
\v 18 And she uncovered her prostitutions, and she uncovered her nakedness, and my soul turned away from her, just as my soul had turned away from her sister.
\v 19 And she multiplied her prostitutions, to remember the days of her youth when she prostituted in the land of Egypt.
\v 20 And she lusted toward their concubines, who the flesh of donkeys {was} their flesh and the emission of horses {was} their emission.
\v 21 And you noted the obscenity of your youth, when {those} from Egypt handled your nipples, for the sake of the breasts of your youth.
\p
\v 22 Therefore, Oholibah, thus says the Lord Yahweh: ‘Behold me!—rousing your lovers against you, those who your soul turned away from them. So I will bring them against you from all around:
\v 23 the sons of Babylon and all the Chaldeans, Pekod and Shoa and Koa, all the sons of Assyria with them, young men of desire, governors and prefects, all of them captains and called {ones}, riders of horses, all of them.
\v 24 And they will come against you with weaponry of a chariot and a wheel, and with an assembly of peoples. A large shield and a shield and a helmet they will set against you all around. And I will place to their face judgment, and they will judge you with their judgments.
\v 25 And I will place my jealousy against you, so they will do with you in heat. Your nose and your ears they will remove, and your remainder will fall by the sword. They—your sons and your daughters they will take, and your remainder will be devoured by the fire.
\v 26 And they will strip you of your garments, and they will take the vessels of your beauty.
\v 27 And I will make your obscenity cease from you and your prostitution from the land of Egypt. Then you will not lift your eyes to them, and Egypt you will not remember again.’
\p
\v 28 For thus says the Lord Yahweh: Behold me!—giving you into the hand of those whom you hated, into the hand of those who your soul turned away from them,
\v 29 (and they will do with you in hatred, and they will take all your labor, and they will leave you, naked and bare; and the nakedness of your prostitutions will be uncovered, and your obscenity and your prostitutions)
\v 30 doing these things to you in exchange for your prostituting after the nations, because you became unclean with their idols.
\v 31 In the way of your sister, you have walked. So I will give her cup into your hand.’
\p
\v 32 Thus says the Lord Yahweh: ‘The cup of your sister you will drink, the deep and the wide {one}; it will be for laughter and for mocking, containing much.
\v 33 {With} drunkenness and sorrow, you will be filled—the cup of horror and desolation, the cup of your sister, Samaria.
\v 34 And you will drink it, and you will drain {it}, and its shards you will gnaw, and your breasts you will tear; for I, I have spoken’—the declaration of the Lord Yahweh.
\p
\v 35 Therefore, thus says the Lord Yahweh: ‘Because you have forgotten me and you have thrown me behind your back, so you also—you will carry your obscenity and your prostitutions.”
\p
\v 36 Then Yahweh said to me, “Son of man, will you judge Oholah and Oholibah? Then declare to them their abominations.
\v 37 For they have committed adultery, and blood {is} on their hands; and {with} their idols, they have committed adultery. And even their sons whom they bore to me they made pass through to them for food.
\v 38 Still this they did to me: They made my sanctuary unclean on that day, and my Sabbaths they profaned.
\v 39 And when they slaughtered their sons to their idols, then they came to my sanctuary on that day to profane it. And behold! Thus they did in the midst of my house.
\v 40 And indeed, for they sent for men coming from a distance, who a messenger was sent to them; and behold! They came—{those} for whom you washed, you painted your eyes, and you adorned yourself {with} ornaments.
\v 41 And you sat on a bed of glory, with a table was arranged to its face, and my incense and my oil you set on it.
\v 42 And the sound of a multitude at ease {was} in her, and to the men from the multitude of humanity, drunkards were brought from the wilderness, and they put bracelets on their hands and a crown of beauty on their heads.
\p
\v 43 And I said of the one worn out {with} adulteries, ‘Now, he will prostitute her prostitutions, and she.’
\v 44 And he went in to her as one goes in to a prostituting woman; thus they went in to Oholah and to Oholibah, the women of obscenity.
\v 45 But righteous men—they will judge them {with} the judgment of adulteresses and {with} the judgment of {ones} pouring blood, for they are adulteresses, and blood {is} on their hands.
\p
\v 46 For thus says the Lord Yahweh: ‘Raise up against them an assembly, and give them to terror and to plunder.
\v 47 And an assembly will stone them with stones, and they will cut them down with their swords. Their sons and their daughters they will kill, and their houses with fire they will burn.
\v 48 So I will make obscenity cease from the land, and all the women will be warned, so they will not do according to your obscenity.
\v 49 And they will put your obscenity on you, and the sins of your idols you will carry. Then you will know that I {am} the Lord Yahweh.’”
\c 24
\p
\v 1 And the word of Yahweh was to me in the ninth year, in the tenth month, on the tenth of the month, saying,
\v 2 “Son of man, write for yourself the name of the day, this very day. The king of Babylon has pressed against Jerusalem on this very day.
\v 3 And speak a proverb to the house of rebellion, and you shall say to them, ‘Thus says the Lord Yahweh:
\q1 “Set on the pot, set {it} on,
\q2 and also pour into it water.
\q1 \v 4 Gather its pieces into it,
\q2 every good piece,
\q1 thigh and shoulder;
\q2 {with} the choicest of bones, fill {it}!
\q1 \v 5 the choicest of the flock take,
\q2 and also stack the bones under it.
\q1 Boil its boilings;
\q2 also its bones have boiled in its midst.”
\p
\v 6 Therefore, thus says the Lord Yahweh:
\q1 “Woe {to} the city of bloods,
\q2 the pot that rust {is} in it,
\q2 but the rust has not gone out from it!
\q1 To its pieces, to its pieces, bring it out;
\q2 a lot has not fallen on it.
\b
\q1 \v 7 For her blood is in her midst;
\q2 on {the} bare surface of a rock, she placed it.
\q1 She did not pour it on the ground,
\q2 to cover over it {with} dust.
\q1 \v 8 To make heat ascend, to avenge vengeance,
\q2 I have put her blood on the bare surface of a rock,
\q2 without it being covered.”
\p
\v 9 Therefore, thus says the Lord Yahweh:
\q1 “Woe {to} the city of bloodshed!
\q2 Also I, I will grow the pile.
\q1 \v 10 Multiply the wood, kindle the fire,
\q2 finishing the flesh and mixing the spice mixture,
\q2 and the bones—let them be burned.
\q1 \v 11 And make it stand on its coals, empty,
\q2 so that it becomes hot and its bronze burns,
\q1 and its uncleanness is poured in its midst;
\q2 its rot ceases.
\q1 \v 12 {With} toil, it has wearied,
\q2 and the abundance of its rot has not gone out from it;
\q2 into a fire, its rust!
\m
\v 13 In your uncleanness {is} obscenity. Because I cleansed you, but you were not clean, from your uncleanness you will not be clean again until I have laid my heat on you.
\v 14 I, Yahweh, have spoken. It is coming, and I will do {it}. I will not refrain, and I will not have pity, and I will not relent. According to your ways and according to your deeds, they have judged you’— the declaration of the Lord Yahweh.”
\p
\v 15 And the word of Yahweh was to me, saying,
\v 16 “Son of man, behold me—taking from you the delight of your eyes with a plague. But you shall not mourn, and you shall not weep, and your tears shall not come.
\v 17 Groan, be silent; {for} the dead, you will not make mourning. Bind your turban on yourself, and your sandals you shall put on your feet, and you shall not cover over {your} mustache, and the bread of men you shall not eat.”
\v 18 And I spoke to the people in the morning, and my wife died in the evening. And I did in the morning just as I was commanded.
\v 19 And the people said to me, “Will you not declare to us what these are to us, that you are doing?”
\v 20 And I said to them, “The word of Yahweh was to me, saying,
\v 21 ‘Say to the house of Israel, “Thus says the Lord Yahweh: ‘Behold me—profaning my sanctuary, the pride of your strength, the desire of your eyes, and the longing of your soul. And your sons and your daughters whom you have left will fall by the sword.
\v 22 And you will do just as I have done. Over {your} mustache, you will not cover, and the bread of men, you will not eat.
\v 23 And {with} your turbans on your heads and {with} your sandals on your feet, you will not mourn, and you will not weep. But you will rot in your iniquities, and you will groan, a man to his brother.
\v 24 And Ezekiel will be for you as a sign; according to all that he has done, you will do. When it comes, then you will know that I {am} the Lord Yahweh.’”’
\p
\v 25 “But you, son of man, will it not {be}, on the day of my taking from them their stronghold, the joy of their splendor, the desire of their eyes, and the lifting up of their soul, their sons and their daughters—
\v 26 on that day, the survivor will come to you, to cause ears to hear?
\v 27 On that day, your mouth will be opened {to} the survivor, and you will speak, and you will no longer be mute. And you will be to them as a sign. Then they will know that I {am} Yahweh.”
\c 25
\p
\v 1 And the word of Yahweh came to me, saying,
\v 2 “Son of man, set your face to the sons of Ammon, and prophesy against them.
\v 3 And you will say to the sons of Ammon, ‘Hear the word of the Lord Yahweh! Thus says the Lord Yahweh: “Because of your saying, ‘Aha!’ to my sanctuary because it was profaned, and to the land of Israel because it was desolated, and to the house of Judah because they went into exile—
\v 4 therefore, behold, I am giving you to the sons of the east as a possession. And they will set their encampments in you, and they will put their dwellings in you. They, they will eat your fruit, and they, they will drink your milk.
\v 5 And I will give Rabbah as a pasture of camels and the sons of Ammon as a resting place of flocks. And you will know that I am Yahweh.”
\p
\v 6 For thus says the Lord Yahweh: “Because of your clapping the hand and your stamping with the foot, and you rejoiced with all of your contempt in the soul to the land of Israel—
\v 7 therefore, behold, I have stretched out my hand against you, and I will give you as plunder to the nations. \f + \ft The written text has a rare word of uncertain meaning; the reading tradition has \fqa plunder\fqa*.\f* And I will cut you off from the peoples, and I will make you perish from the lands. I will destroy you, and you will know that I am Yahweh.”
\p
\v 8 Thus says the Lord Yahweh: “Because of the saying of Moab and Seir, ‘Behold, the house of Judah is like all of the nations,’
\v 9 therefore, behold, I am opening the shoulder of Moab from the cities, from his cities, from his end, the splendor of the land: Beth Jeshimoth, Baal Meon, and Kiriathaim,
\v 10 to the sons of the east along with the sons of Ammon. And I will give it as a possession, so that the sons of Ammon will not be remembered among the nations.
\v 11 And against Moab I will do judgments, and they will know that I am Yahweh.”
\p
\v 12 Thus says the Lord Yahweh: “Because of the doing of Edom in avenging vengeance against the house of Judah, and they became guilty, being guilty, and they took vengeance on them”—
\v 13 therefore thus says the Lord Yahweh: “I will stretch out my hand against Edom, and I will cut off from her man and beast. And I will make her a waste from Teman, and to Dedan they will fall by the sword.
\v 14 And I will give my vengeance on Edom by the hand of my people Israel, and they will do in Edom according to my anger and according to my wrath. And they will know my vengeance”— the declaration of the Lord Yahweh.
\p
\v 15 Thus says the Lord Yahweh: “Because of the doing of the Philistines in vengeance, and they avenged vengeance with contempt in the soul, for destruction {with} everlasting hostility”—
\v 16 therefore thus says the Lord Yahweh: “Behold, I am stretching out my hand against the Philistines, and I will cut off the Cherethites, and I will make the remnant of the shore of the sea perish.
\v 17 And I will do great vengeances against them with rebukes of wrath. And they will know that I am Yahweh when I put my vengeance on them.”’”
\c 26
\p
\v 1 Now it happened in the eleventh year, on the first of the month, the word of Yahweh came to me, saying,
\v 2 “Son of man, because Tyre has said against Jerusalem, ‘Aha! The doors of the peoples have been broken. She has been turned to me. I will be filled; she has been laid waste!’—
\v 3 therefore thus says the Lord Yahweh: ‘Behold, I am against you, Tyre, and I will bring up against you many nations, as the sea brings up its waves.
\v 4 And they will destroy the walls of Tyre and tear down her towers. And I will scrape her dust from her, and I will make her as a bare surface of a rock.
\v 5 A spreading place of nets she will be in the midst of the sea, for I, I have spoken’—‘the declaration of the Lord Yahweh. ‘And she will become plunder for the nations.
\v 6 And her daughters who are in the field will be killed by the sword. And they will know that I am Yahweh.’
\p
\v 7 For thus says the Lord Yahweh: ‘Behold, I am bringing to Tyre Nebuchadnezzar the king of Babylon from the north, a king of kings, with horse and with chariot and with horsemen, and an assembly and a great people.
\v 8 Your daughters in the field he will kill by the sword. And he will set a siege wall against you, and he will pour out a siege mound against you, and he will raise up a large shield against you.
\v 9 And the blow of his battering ram he will set against your walls, and your towers he will break down with his swords.
\v 10 From the abundance of his horses their dust will cover you. From the sound of horseman and wheel and chariot your walls will shake, when he comes into your gates like the entrances of a city broken open.
\v 11 With the hooves of his horses he will trample all of your streets. Your people he will kill by the sword, and the pillars of your strength will go down to the ground.
\v 12 And they will spoil your wealth and plunder your merchandise, and they will tear down your walls and break down the houses of your desire. And your stones and your wood and your dust they will put in the midst of the water.
\v 13 And I will make the multitude of your songs cease, and the sound of your harps will not be heard again.
\v 14 And I will give you as a bare surface of a rock. A spreading place of nets you will be. You will not be built again, for I, Yahweh, have spoken’— the declaration of the Lord Yahweh.
\p
\v 15 Thus says the Lord Yahweh to Tyre: ‘Will not the coastlands shake from the sound of your fall, when the slain one groans, when slaughter is slain in your midst?
\v 16 And all of the princes of the sea will come down from upon their thrones, and they will remove their robes, and they will strip off their garments of embroidery. Tremblings they will put on; on the ground they will sit, and they will tremble at moments, and they will be desolate over you.
\v 17 And they will take up a lamentation over you, and they will say to you,
\q1 “How you have perished, O inhabited one from the seas,
\q2 the praised city, which was strong in the sea, she and her inhabitants,
\q2 who put their terror on all of her inhabitants!
\q1 \v 18 Now the coastlands will tremble on the day of your fall,
\q2 and the coastlands that are in the sea will be terrified from your going out.”’
\p
\v 19 For thus says the Lord Yahweh: ‘When I make you a city laid waste, like the cities that have not been inhabited, when {I} bring up the deep over you and the many waters cover you,
\v 20 then I will bring you down with the ones going down to the pit, to a people of eternity. And I will make you dwell in the land of the lower parts, like ruins from eternity, with the ones going down to the pit, so that you will not dwell {there}. And I will put splendor in the land of the living.
\v 21 I will give you terrors, and you {will} be no more. And you will be sought, but you will not be found again forever’— the declaration of the Lord Yahweh.”
\c 27
\p
\v 1 And the word of Yahweh came to me, saying,
\v 2 “And you, son of man, take up over Tyre a lamentation,
\v 3 and you shall say to Tyre, the dweller at the entrances of the sea, the merchant of the peoples to many coastlands, thus says the Lord Yahweh:
\q1 ‘Tyre, you, you have said,
\q2 “I am perfect of beauty.”
\q1 \v 4 In the heart of the seas are your borders;
\q2 your builders perfected your beauty.
\q1 \v 5 They built all of the planks for you with cypresses from Senir;
\q2 they took a cedar from Lebanon to make a mast upon you.
\q1 \v 6 They made oaks from Bashan {into} your oars;
\q2 they made your deck {of} ivory, the daughter of Ashurim, from the coasts of Kittim.
\q1 \v 7 Your sail was fine linen with embroidery from Egypt, to be for you as a banner;
\q2 your covering was blue and purple from the coasts of Elishah.
\q1 \v 8 The dwellers of Sidon and Arvad were rowers for you;
\q2 your wise men, O Tyre, were in you;
\q2 they were your rope-men.
\q1 \v 9 The elders of Gebal and her wise men were in you, the strengtheners of your cracks.
\q2 All of the ships of the sea and their sailors were in you to exchange your merchandise.
\q1 \v 10 Persia and Lud and Put were in your army, your men of war.
\q2 Shield and helmet they hung in you;
\q2 they, they gave your splendor.
\q1 \v 11 The sons of Arvad and your army were on your walls all around, and Gammadim were in your towers.
\q2 Their shields they hung on your walls all around;
\q2 they, they perfected your beauty.
\p
\v 12 Tarshish was your trader from the abundance of all wealth; they gave your wares with silver, iron, tin, and lead.
\v 13 Javan, Tubal, and Meshech, they, they were your merchants; with the soul of man and vessels of bronze they gave your merchandise.
\v 14 From Beth Togarmah they gave horses and warhorses and mules {as} your wares.
\v 15 The sons of Dedan were your merchants; many coastlands were the trade of your hand. They brought back horns of ivory and ebony {as} your gift.
\v 16 Aram was your trader from the abundance of your works; with emerald, purple, and embroidery, and fine linen, and corals, and ruby they gave in your wares.
\v 17 Judah and the land of Israel, they, they were your merchants; with wheat of Minnith and pannag and honey and oil and balm they gave your merchandise.
\v 18 Damascus was your trader in the abundance of your works, from the abundance of all wealth, with wine of Helbon and wool of whiteness.
\v 19 Vedan and Javan from Uzal gave in your wares; wrought iron, cassia, and cane were in your merchandise.
\v 20 Dedan was your merchant with garments of covering for riding.
\v 21 Arabia and all of the princes of Kedar, they, they were the traders of your hand; with lambs and rams and male goats, in them {were} your traders.
\v 22 The merchants of Sheba and Raamah, they, they were your merchants; with the head of every spice and with every precious stone and gold they gave your wares.
\v 23 Haran and Kanneh and Eden, the merchants of Sheba, Assyria, {and} Kilmad were your merchant.
\v 24 They, they were your merchants with choice garments, with wrappings of blue and embroidery, and with coverings of multicolored cloth bound with cords and made firm, in your marketplace.
\v 25 The ships of Tarshish were your travelers {with} your merchandise.
\q1 And you were filled
\q2 and you became very heavy in the heart of the seas.
\q1 \v 26 Into many waters the ones rowing you brought you;
\q2 the wind of the east broke you in the heart of the seas.
\q1 \v 27 Your wealth and your wares, your merchandise, your sailors and your rope-men,
\q2 the strengtheners of your cracks and the ones exchanging your merchandise,
\q2 and all of your men of war who are in you, and with all of your assembly that is in your midst,
\q2 they will fall in the heart of the seas on the day of your fall.
\q1 \v 28 At the sound of the cry of your rope-men
\q2 the pasturelands will shake.
\q1 \v 29 And all of the graspers of an oar will come down from their ships;
\q2 the sailors, all of the rope-men of the sea,
\q2 will stand on the land.
\q1 \v 30 And they will make heard over you with their voice,
\q2 and they will cry out bitterly, and they will bring up dust on their heads;
\q2 in the ashes they will roll.
\q1 \v 31 And they will make themselves bald for you {with} a baldness,
\q2 and they will gird sackcloth, and they will weep for you in bitterness of soul, a bitter mourning.
\q1 \v 32 And they will take up over you in their wailing a lamentation, and they will lament over you:
\q2 “Who is like Tyre, like a silenced one in the midst of the sea?”
\q1 \v 33 When your wares went out from the seas, you satisfied many peoples;
\q2 with the abundance of your wealth and your merchandise you made rich the kings of the earth.
\q1 \v 34 {At this} time {you} are broken from the seas, in the depths of waters,
\q2 your merchandise and all of your assembly in your midst have fallen.
\q1 \v 35 All of the dwellers of the coastlands are desolate over you,
\q2 and their kings have shuddered a shudder;
\q2 {their} faces have quaked.
\q1 \v 36 Traders among the peoples hiss over you;
\q2 terrors you have become, and you are no more forever.’”
\c 28
\p
\v 1 And the word of Yahweh came to me, saying,
\v 2 “Son of man, say to the ruler of Tyre, ‘Thus says the Lord Yahweh, “Because your heart has been high, and you have said, ‘I am God; {in} the dwelling of God I have dwelt in the heart of the seas,’ and you are man and not God, and you have given your heart as the heart of God.
\v 3 Behold, you are wiser than Daniel; every hidden thing they have not darkened {from} you.
\v 4 By your wisdom and by your understanding you have made for yourself wealth, and you have made gold and silver in your treasuries.
\v 5 By the abundance of your wisdom, by your merchandise, you have increased your wealth, and your heart became high in your wealth.”
\p
\v 6 Therefore thus says the Lord Yahweh, “Because of your giving your heart as the heart of God—
\v 7 therefore, behold, I am bringing against you strangers, the ruthless of the nations. And they will draw out their swords against the beauty of your wisdom, and they will profane your radiance.
\v 8 They will bring you down to the pit, and you will die the deaths of a slain one in the heart of the seas.
\v 9 Saying, will you say, ‘I am God,’ to the face of the ones killing you? And you are man and not God in the hand of the ones piercing you.
\v 10 The deaths of uncircumcised ones you will die by the hand of strangers, for I, I have spoken”— the declaration of the Lord Yahweh.’”
\p
\v 11 And the word of Yahweh came to me, saying,
\v 12 “Son of man, take up a lamentation over the king of Tyre, and you shall say to him, ‘Thus says the Lord Yahweh, “You were the one sealing a pattern, full of wisdom and perfect of beauty.
\v 13 In Eden, the garden of God, you were. Every precious stone was your covering: ruby, topaz, and diamond, beryl, onyx, and jasper, sapphire, emerald, and garnet; and gold. The work of your tambourines and your sockets was in you. In the day of your being created they were established.
\v 14 You were a cherub of anointing, the one covering. And I placed you, you were on the mountain of the holiness of God; you walked about in the midst of the stones of fire.
\v 15 You were blameless in your ways from the day of your being created until injustice was found in you.
\v 16 They filled your midst {with} violence in the abundance of your merchandise, and you sinned. And I profaned you from the mountain of God, and I made you perish, O cherub, the one covering, from the midst of the stones of fire.
\v 17 Your heart was high in your beauty; you corrupted your wisdom on account of your radiance. On the earth I threw you; to the face of kings I gave you, to look upon you.
\v 18 From the abundance of your iniquities, in the injustice of your merchandise, you profaned your sanctuaries. And I brought out fire from your midst; it, it consumed you. And I gave you as ashes on the earth before the eyes of all the ones seeing you.
\v 19 All of the ones knowing you among the peoples are desolate over you. You have become terrors, and you are no more forever.’”
\p
\v 20 And the word of Yahweh came to me, saying,
\v 21 “Son of man, set your face against Sidon, and prophesy against her.
\v 22 And you shall say, ‘Thus says the Lord Yahweh, “Behold, I am against you, Sidon, and I will be glorified in your midst. And they will know that I am Yahweh when I do judgments in her and I am sanctified in her.
\v 23 And I will send into her plague and blood in her streets, and the slain one will fall in her midst by the sword against her from all around. And they will know that I am Yahweh.
\v 24 And there will no longer be for the house of Israel a pricking brier and a thorn causing pain from all of those around them, the ones despising them. And they will know that I am the Lord Yahweh.”
\p
\v 25 Thus says the Lord Yahweh, “When I gather the house of Israel from the peoples among whom they were scattered, and I am sanctified in them before the eyes of the nations, then they will dwell on their dirt that I gave to my servant, to Jacob.
\v 26 And they will dwell on it in security, and they will build houses and plant vineyards. And they will dwell in security when I do judgments on all of those despising them from around them. And they will know that I am Yahweh their God.”’”
\c 29
\p
\v 1 In the tenth year, in the tenth {month}, on the twelfth of the month, the word of Yahweh came to me, saying,
\v 2 “Son of man, set your face against Pharaoh the king of Egypt, and prophesy against him and against Egypt, all of it.
\v 3 Speak and say, ‘Thus says the Lord Yahweh, “Behold, I am against you, Pharaoh king of Egypt, the great sea monster lying in the midst of his rivers, who said, ‘To me {is} my Nile, and I, I have made myself.’
\v 4 And I will put hooks in your jaws, and I will make the fish of your rivers cling to your scales. And I will bring you up from the midst of your rivers, and all of the fish of your rivers will cling to your scales.
\v 5 And I will cast you out to the wilderness, you and all of the fish of your rivers. You will fall on the face of the field; you will not be gathered, nor will you be gathered together. I have given you as food to the living thing of the land and to the bird of the heavens.
\v 6 And all of the inhabitants of Egypt will know that I am Yahweh, because of their being a staff of reed for the house of Israel.
\v 7 When they grasped you by your palm, you were crushed, and you split open for them every shoulder. And when they leaned on you, you were broken, and you made all of their loins shake.”
\p
\v 8 Therefore, thus says the Lord Yahweh, “Behold, I am bringing against you a sword, and I will cut off from you man and beast.
\v 9 And the land of Egypt will become a desolation and a ruin. And they will know that I am Yahweh, because he said, ‘The Nile is mine, and I, I have made {it}.’
\v 10 Therefore, behold, I am against you and against your rivers, and I will make the land of Egypt into ruins of devastation, a desolation, from Migdol {to} Syene and as far as the border of Cush.
\v 11 The foot of man will not pass through it, and the foot of beast will not pass through it, and it will not be inhabited 40 years.
\v 12 And I will make the land of Egypt a desolation in the midst of desolated lands, and her cities will be a desolation in the midst of cities laid waste, 40 years. And I will scatter Egypt among the nations and disperse them among the lands.”
\p
\v 13 For thus says the Lord Yahweh, “From the end of 40 years I will gather Egypt from the peoples where they were scattered.
\v 14 And I will restore the fortunes of Egypt, and I will bring them back {to} the land of Pathros, to the land of their origin. And they will be there a lowly kingdom.
\v 15 It will be the lowliest from the kingdoms, and it will not lift itself up again over the nations. And I will make them few, so as not to rule over the nations.
\v 16 And it will no longer be for the house of Israel as a confidence, bringing iniquity to remembrance when they turned after them. And they will know that I am the Lord Yahweh.”’”
\p
\v 17 And it happened in the twenty-seventh year, in the first {month}, on the first of the month, the word of Yahweh came to me, saying,
\v 18 “Son of man, Nebuchadnezzar the king of Babylon made his army serve a great service against Tyre. Every head was made bald, and every shoulder was made bare. But there were no wages for him and for his army from Tyre for the service that he served against her.
\p
\v 19 Therefore, thus says the Lord Yahweh, ‘Behold, I am giving to Nebuchadnezzar the king of Babylon the land of Egypt. And he will carry away her multitude, and he will plunder her plunder, and he will spoil her spoil. And it will be wages for his army.
\v 20 {As} his wages for which he served against her, I have given to him the land of Egypt, because they did {it} for me’— the declaration of the Lord Yahweh.
\p
\v 21 In that day I will make a horn sprout for the house of Israel, and I will give an opening of mouth to you in their midst. And they will know that I am Yahweh.”
\c 30
\p
\v 1 And the word of Yahweh came to me, saying,
\v 2 “Son of man, prophesy and say, ‘Thus says the Lord Yahweh, “Wail, ‘Alas for the day!’
\v 3 For a day is near, and a day is near for Yahweh, a day of cloud; a time of nations it will be.
\v 4 And a sword will come into Egypt, and there will be anguish in Cush when the slain fall in Egypt, and they take her multitude, and her foundations are torn down.
\p
\v 5 Cush and Put and Lud and all the mixed company and Cub, and the sons of the land of the covenant with them— by the sword they will fall.”
\p
\v 6 Thus says Yahweh, “And the supporters of Egypt will fall, and the pride of her strength will go down. From Migdol {to} Syene they will fall by the sword in her”— the declaration of the Lord Yahweh.
\m
\v 7 “And they will be desolated in the midst of desolated lands, and his cities will be in the midst of cities laid waste.
\v 8 And they will know that I am Yahweh when I put fire in Egypt and all of her helpers are broken.
\v 9 In that day messengers will go out from my face in ships to make Cush tremble {in its} security, and there will be anguish among them in the day of Egypt; for behold, it is coming.”
\p
\v 10 Thus says the Lord Yahweh, “And I will make the multitude of Egypt cease by the hand of Nebuchadnezzar the king of Babylon.
\v 11 He and his people with him, the ruthless of the nations, are being brought to destroy the land. And they will draw out their swords against Egypt and fill the land with the slain.
\v 12 And I will make the rivers dry ground, and I will sell the land into the hand of evil ones, and I will make the land and its fullness desolate by the hand of strangers.” I, Yahweh, have spoken.
\p
\v 13 Thus says the Lord Yahweh, “And I will make idols perish, and I will make worthless idols cease from Memphis, and there will no longer be a prince from the land of Egypt. And I will put fear in the land of Egypt.
\v 14 And I will make Pathros desolate, and I will put fire in Zoan, and I will do judgments in On.
\v 15 And I will pour out my wrath on Sin, the fortress of Egypt, and I will cut off the multitude of On.
\v 16 And I will put fire in Egypt. Writhing Sin will writhe, and On will be for being broken open, and Memphis {will have} adversaries by day.
\v 17 The young men of Aven and Pi Beseth will fall by the sword, and they, they will go into captivity.
\v 18 And in Tahpanhes the day will grow dark, when I break there the yokes of Egypt, and the pride of her strength will cease in her. She, a cloud will cover her, and her daughters will go into captivity.
\v 19 And I will do judgments in Egypt, and they will know that I am Yahweh.”’”
\p
\v 20 Now it happened in the eleventh year, in the first {month}, on the seventh of the month, the word of Yahweh came to me, saying,
\v 21 “Son of man, I have broken the arm of Pharaoh the king of Egypt. And behold, it has not been bound up, to give medicines, to put a bandage to bind it up, for it to be strong to grasp the sword.
\p
\v 22 Therefore thus says the Lord Yahweh, ‘Behold, I am to Pharaoh the king of Egypt, and I will break his arms, the strong one and the broken one, and I will make the sword fall from his hand.
\v 23 And I will scatter Egypt among the nations, and I will disperse them among the lands.
\v 24 And I will strengthen the arms of the king of Babylon, and I will put my sword in his hand. And I will break the arms of Pharaoh, and he will groan the groanings of a slain one to his face.
\v 25 And I will make strong the arms of the king of Babylon, and the arms of Pharaoh will fall. And they will know that I am Yahweh when I put my sword into the hand of the king of Babylon, and he stretches it out against the land of Egypt.
\v 26 And I will scatter Egypt among the nations, and I will disperse them among the lands. And they will know that I am Yahweh.’”
\c 31
\p
\v 1 Now it happened in the eleventh year, in the third {month}, on the first of the month, the word of Yahweh came to me, saying,
\v 2 “Son of man, say to Pharaoh the king of Egypt and to his multitude, ‘To whom are you like in your greatness?
\v 3 Behold, Assyria was a cedar in Lebanon, beautiful of branch and a forest giving shade and high of height, and among the thick boughs was its top.
\v 4 Waters made it great; the deep made it high, with its rivers going around its planting, and its channels it sent out to all the trees of the field.
\v 5 Therefore its height was higher than all of the trees of the field, and its limbs became many, and its boughs grew long from many waters in its sending out.
\v 6 Every bird of the heavens nested in its limbs, and every beast of the field gave birth under its boughs, and all of the many nations dwelt in its shade.
\v 7 And it became beautiful in its greatness, in the length of its branches, for its root was by many waters.
\v 8 Cedars did not darken it in the garden of God; cypresses were not like its limbs, and plane trees were not like its boughs. Not any tree in the garden of God was like it in its beauty.
\v 9 I made it beautiful, in the abundance of its branches, and all the trees of Eden that were in the garden of God envied it.
\p
\v 10 Therefore thus says the Lord Yahweh, “Because it was high in height, and it set its top among the thick boughs, and its heart was high in its height,
\v 11 and I gave it into the hand of a mighty one of the nations; doing he did to it. According to its wickedness I drove it out.
\v 12 And strangers, the ruthless of the nations, cut it down and they abandoned it. Its branches fell on the mountains and in all the valleys, and its boughs were broken in all the channels of the land. And all the peoples of the land went down from its shade and abandoned it.
\v 13 Every bird of the heavens would dwell on its ruin, and every beast of the field was at its boughs,
\p
\v 14 so that all the trees of waters will not be high in their height, and they will not set their top among the thick boughs, and their mighty ones will not stand in their height— all of the drinkers of waters. For all of them have been given to death, to the lower land, in the midst of the sons of man, to the ones going down to the pit.”
\p
\v 15 Thus says the Lord Yahweh, “In the day of its going down to Sheol I caused mourning. I covered the deep over it, and I withheld its rivers, and many waters were restrained. And I made Lebanon dark over it, and all the trees of the field were faint over it.
\v 16 I made nations quake from the sound of its downfall, in my bringing it down to Sheol with the ones going down to the pit. And all the trees of Eden were comforted in the lower land, the choicest and good of Lebanon, all of the drinkers of waters.
\v 17 They also, with it, went down to Sheol, to the slain of the sword, and its arm— they dwelt in its shade in the midst of the nations.
\v 18 To whom are you thus like, in glory and in greatness, among the trees of Eden? But you will be brought down with the trees of Eden to the lower land. In the midst of the uncircumcised you will lie down with the slain of the sword. That is Pharaoh and all of his multitude”— the declaration of the Lord Yahweh.’”
\c 32
\p
\v 1 Now it happened in the twelfth year, in the twelfth month, on the first of the month, the word of Yahweh came to me, saying,
\v 2 “Son of man, take up a lamentation over Pharaoh the king of Egypt, and say to him, ‘You were likened to a young lion of the nations, but you are like the sea monster in the seas. And you burst forth in your rivers, and you stirred up the waters with your feet, and you muddied their rivers.
\v 3 Thus says the Lord Yahweh, “And I will spread my net over you in an assembly of many peoples, and they will bring you up in my dragnet.
\v 4 And I will throw you on the land; I will hurl you on the face of the field. And I will make every bird of the heavens dwell on you, and I will make the living thing of all the land satisfied from you.
\v 5 And I will put your flesh on the mountains, and I will fill the valleys with your carcass.
\v 6 And I will make the land of your outflow drink from your blood, to the mountains, and the channels will be filled from you.
\v 7 And I will cover the heavens at your extinguishing, and I will make their stars dark. The sun, with a cloud I will cover it, and the moon will not make its light shine.
\v 8 I will make all of the luminaries of light in the heavens dark over you, and I will put darkness on your land”— the declaration of the Lord Yahweh.
\v 9 “And I will provoke the heart of many peoples to anger in my bringing your breaking among the nations, to lands that you have not known.
\v 10 And I will make many peoples desolate over you, and their kings will shudder a shuddering over you, in my making my sword fly over their faces. And they will tremble for moments, a man for his soul, in the day of your downfall.”
\p
\v 11 For thus says the Lord Yahweh, “The sword of the king of Babylon will come to you.
\v 12 I will make your multitude fall by the swords of warriors, the ruthless of the nations, all of them. And they will devastate the pride of Egypt, and all of her multitude will be destroyed.
\v 13 And I will make all of her beasts perish from beside many waters, and the foot of man will not stir them up again, and the hooves of a beast will not stir them up.
\v 14 Then I will make their waters settle, and their rivers I will make go like oil”— the declaration of the Lord Yahweh.
\v 15 “In my making the land of Egypt a desolation, and a land desolated from its fullness, in my striking all of the inhabitants in her— then they will know that I am Yahweh.
\v 16 A lamentation it is, and they will lament it. The daughters of the nations will lament it; over Egypt and over all of her multitude they will lament it”— the declaration of the Lord Yahweh.’”
\p
\v 17 Now it happened in the twelfth year, on the fifteenth of the month, the word of Yahweh came to me, saying,
\v 18 “Son of man, wail over the multitude of Egypt, and bring it down, it and the daughters of majestic nations, to the lower land, with the ones going down to the pit.
\v 19 ‘Than whom are you more pleasant? Go down and be laid down with the uncircumcised!’
\v 20 In the midst of the slain of the sword they will fall. A sword has been given; draw her out and all of her multitudes.
\v 21 The mighty ones of the warriors will speak to him from the midst of Sheol with his helpers, ‘They have gone down; they lie, the uncircumcised, the slain of the sword.’
\v 22 There is Assyria and all of her assembly; all around him are his graves, all of them slain, the fallen by the sword,
\v 23 whose graves have been given in the recesses of the pit, and her assembly is all around her burial place, all of them slain, falling by the sword, who had given terror in the land of the living.
\v 24 There is Elam and all of her multitude, all around her burial place, all of them slain, the fallen by the sword, who went down uncircumcised to the lower land, who had given their terror in the land of the living. And they bore their humiliation with the ones going down to the pit.
\v 25 They have given a bed for her in the midst of the slain among all of her multitude; all around him are her graves. All of them are uncircumcised, slain of the sword, for their terror was given in the land of the living, and they bore their humiliation with the ones going down to the pit. He has been put in the midst of the slain.
\v 26 There are Meshech, Tubal, and all of her multitude; all around him are her graves. All of them are uncircumcised, pierced ones of the sword, for they had given their terror in the land of the living.
\v 27 And they do not lie with the warriors, the ones falling from among the uncircumcised, who went down to Sheol with the weapons of their war. And they put their swords under their heads, and their iniquities were on their bones, for the terror of warriors was in the land of the living.
\v 28 And you, in the midst of the uncircumcised you will be broken, and you will lie with the slain of the sword.
\p
\v 29 There is Edom, her kings and all of her leaders, who have been given, in their might, with the slain of the sword. They, they will lie with the uncircumcised and with the ones going down to the pit.
\v 30 There are the princes of the north, all of them, and every Sidonian, who went down with the slain, ashamed in their terror from their might. And they lay uncircumcised with the slain of the sword, and they bore their humiliation with the ones going down to the pit.
\p
\v 31 Pharaoh will see them and be comforted over all of his multitude— the slain of the sword, Pharaoh and all of his army”— the declaration of the Lord Yahweh.
\v 32 “For I have given his terror in the land of the living, and he will be laid down in the midst of the uncircumcised, with the slain of the sword— Pharaoh and all of his multitude”— the declaration of the Lord Yahweh.
\c 33
\p
\v 1 And the word of Yahweh came to me, saying,
\v 2 “Son of man, speak to the sons of your people and say to them, ‘When I bring a sword against a land, and the people of the land take one man from their number and give him to themselves as a watchman,
\v 3 and he sees the sword coming against the land and blows on the shofar and warns the people,
\v 4 and the hearer hears the sound of the shofar and is not warned, and a sword comes and takes him— his blood will be on his head.
\v 5 The sound of the shofar he heard, and he was not warned; his blood will be on him. But {if} he, being warned, he saves his life.
\p
\v 6 But if the watchman sees the sword coming and does not blow on the shofar, and the people are not warned, and a sword comes and takes a life from them— he, he is taken in his iniquity, but his blood I will demand from the hand of the watchman.’
\p
\v 7 And you, son of man— a watchman I have given you for the house of Israel. And you will hear a word from my mouth, and you will warn them from me.
\v 8 When I say to the wicked one, ‘Wicked one, dying you will die,’ and you do not speak to warn the wicked one from his way— he, the wicked one, will die in his iniquity, but his blood I will seek from your hand.
\v 9 But you, if you warn a wicked one from his way, to turn back from it, and he does not turn back from his way— he, he will die in his iniquity, but you, you have delivered your soul.
\p
\v 10 And you, son of man, say to the house of Israel, ‘Thus you have said, saying, “Surely our transgressions and our sins are upon us, and in them we are rotting away. And how shall we live?”’
\v 11 Say to them, ‘The life of me’— the declaration of the Lord Yahweh—‘if I delight in the death of the wicked one, but rather in the turning back of a wicked one from his way, so that he lives. Turn back, turn back from your evil ways! And why should you die, house of Israel?’
\p
\v 12 And you, son of man, say to the sons of your people, ‘The righteousness of the righteous will not deliver him in the day of his transgression, and the wickedness of the wicked— he will not stumble by it in the day of his turning back from his wickedness. And a righteous one will not be able to live by it in the day of his sinning.
\v 13 When I say to the righteous, “Living he will live,” and he, he trusts in his righteousness and does injustice— all his righteousness will not be remembered, and in his injustice that he did, in it he will die.
\v 14 When I say to the wicked, “Dying you will die,” and he turns back from his sin and does justice and righteousness—
\v 15 the wicked returns a pledge, he repays robbery, he walks in the statutes of life, so as not to do injustice— living he will live; he will not die.
\v 16 All his sin that he sinned will not be remembered for him. He has done justice and righteousness; living he will live.
\p
\v 17 But the sons of your people say, “The way of the Lord is not fair,” but they, their way is not fair.
\v 18 In the turning back of a righteous one from his righteousness, and he does injustice— then he will die in them.
\v 19 And in the turning back of a wicked one from his wickedness, and he does justice and righteousness— because of them he, he will live.
\v 20 But you say, “The way of the Lord is not fair.” A man according to his ways I will judge you, house of Israel.’”
\p
\v 21 Now it happened in the twelfth year of our exile, in the tenth {month}, on the fifth of the month, the fugitive came to me from Jerusalem, saying, “The city has been struck.”
\v 22 Now the hand of Yahweh was to me in the evening, to the face of the coming of the fugitive, and he opened my mouth until the coming to me in the morning. And my mouth was opened, and I was not mute any longer.
\p
\v 23 And the word of Yahweh came to me, saying,
\v 24 “Son of man, the dwellers of these ruins on the land of Israel are saying, saying, ‘Abraham was one, and he possessed the land, but we are many; to us the land has been given as a possession.’
\p
\v 25 Therefore say to them, ‘Thus says the Lord Yahweh: You eat upon the blood, and you lift up your eyes to your idols, and you shed blood—and will you possess the land?
\v 26 You have stood upon your sword; you have done an abomination; and a man, the wife of his neighbor you have defiled— and will you possess the land?’
\p
\v 27 Thus you will say to them, ‘Thus says the Lord Yahweh, “The life of me, if not that they will fall by the sword in the ruins, and that I will give him on the face of the field to the living thing to eat him, and that they will die by the plague in the strongholds and in the caves.
\v 28 And I will make the land a desolation and a waste, and the pride of her strength will cease, and the mountains of Israel will be desolate, from there being no one passing over.
\v 29 And they will know that I am Yahweh, when I make the land a desolation and a waste on account of all their abominations that they did.’
\p
\v 30 And you, son of man— the sons of your people, the ones speaking with one another about you beside the walls and in the entrances of the houses, and one speaks with one, a man with his brother, saying, ‘Come, please, and hear what the word is that is going out from Yahweh.’
\v 31 And my people come to you like the coming of a people, and they sit to your face, and they hear your words, but them they do not do. For lusts in their mouth they, they are doing; after their gain their heart is going.
\v 32 And behold, you are to them like a song of lusts, beautiful of voice and doing well {at} playing. And they hear your words, but they are not doing them.
\v 33 And in its coming— behold, it is coming— then they will know that a prophet has been in their midst.”
\c 34
\p
\v 1 And the word of Yahweh was to me, saying,
\v 2 “Son of man, prophesy against the shepherds of Israel. Prophesy and you shall say to them, to the shepherds, ‘Thus says the Lord Yahweh: Woe, shepherds of Israel who have been shepherding themselves! Should not the shepherds shepherd the flock?
\v 3 The fat you eat, and the wool you wear; the fat one you slaughter. The flock you do not shepherd.
\v 4 The weak ones you have not strengthened, and the sick one you have not healed, and the broken one you have not bound up, and the one driven away you have not brought back, and the perishing one you have not searched for. And with force you have subjugated them, and with harshness.
\v 5 And they scattered without a shepherd, and they became food for every living thing of the field, and they scattered.
\v 6 My flock stray on all of the mountains and on every high hill, and over all of the face of the land my flock were scattered, and there is no one seeking, and there is no one searching.
\p
\v 7 Therefore, shepherds, hear the word of Yahweh:
\v 8 {By} my life—the declaration of the Lord Yahweh—If {it is} not because of my flock becoming prey, and my flock has become food for every living thing of the field from there being no shepherd, and my shepherds did not seek my flock, and the shepherds shepherded themselves and they did not shepherd my flock—
\p
\v 9 therefore, shepherds, hear the word of Yahweh:
\v 10 Thus says the Lord Yahweh: Behold me, against the shepherds! And I will seek my flock from their hand, and I will cause them to cease from shepherding the flock, and the shepherds will no longer shepherd themselves. And I will deliver my flock from their mouth, and they will not be food for them.
\p
\v 11 For thus says the Lord Yahweh: Behold me, me, I will seek my flock, and I will attend to them.
\v 12 Like the attending of a shepherd of his flock in the day of his being in the midst of his scattered flock, thus I will attend to my flock. And I will deliver them from all of the places which they were scattered there in a day of cloud and thick darkness.
\v 13 And I will bring them out from the peoples, and I will gather them from the lands, and I will bring them to their land. And I will shepherd them on the mountains of Israel, by the streams and in all of the dwelling places of the land.
\v 14 In a good pasture I will shepherd them, and on the mountains of the height of Israel their habitation will be. There they will lie down in a good habitation, and a fat pasture they will graze among the mountains of Israel.
\v 15 I, I will shepherd my flock, and I, I will make them lie down—the declaration of the Lord Yahweh.
\v 16 The perishing one I will search for, and the one driven away I will bring back, and the broken one I will bind up, and the sick one I will strengthen. But the fat {one} and the strong {one} I will destroy. I will shepherd it with justice.
\p
\v 17 And you, my flock, thus says the Lord Yahweh: Behold me, judging between a sheep and a sheep, {between} the rams and the male goats.
\v 18 {Is it} too little for you {that} you graze the good pasture, and the rest of your pastures you trample with your feet, and you drink the settled waters, and the remaining ones with your feet you muddy?
\v 19 And my flock, the trampling of your feet they graze, and the muddying of your feet they drink.
\p
\v 20 Therefore, thus says the Lord Yahweh to them: Behold me, me, I will judge between a fat sheep and between a lean sheep,
\v 21 because with side and with shoulder you push, and with your horns you gore all of the weak ones, until you have scattered them to the outside.
\v 22 And I will save my flock, and they will no longer be plunder, and I will judge between a sheep and a sheep.
\v 23 And I will raise up over them one shepherd—and he will shepherd them—my servant David. He, he will shepherd them, and he, he will be the shepherd to them.
\v 24 And I, Yahweh, will be God to them, and my servant David {will be} a prince in their midst. I, Yahweh, have spoken.
\p
\v 25 And I will cut for them a covenant of peace, and I will cause the harmful living thing to cease from the land. And they will dwell in the wilderness in security, and they will sleep in the forests.
\v 26 And I will make them and the surroundings of my hill a blessing, and I will bring down the rain in its time. Rains of blessing they will be.
\v 27 And the tree of the field will give its fruit, and the land will give its produce, and they will be on their land in security. And they will know that I {am} Yahweh in my breaking of the bars of their yoke and I will deliver them from the hand of the ones enslaving on them.
\v 28 And they will no longer be plunder for the nations, and the living thing of the land will not eat them. And they will dwell in security, and there will be no one making {them} afraid.
\v 29 And I will raise up for them a planting for a name, and they will no longer be gathered ones of famine in the land, and they will no longer bear the humiliation of the nations.
\v 30 And they will know that I, Yahweh their God, {am} with them, and they {are} my people, the house of Israel—the declaration of the Lord Yahweh.
\v 31 And you {are} my flock, the flock of my pasture. You {are} man. I {am} your God—the declaration of the Lord Yahweh.’”
\c 35
\p
\v 1 And the word of Yahweh was to me, saying,
\v 2 “Son of man, set your face against Mount Seir, and prophesy against it.
\v 3 And you shall say to it, ‘Thus says the Lord Yahweh: Behold me against you, Mount Seir! And I will stretch out my hand against you, and I will make you a desolation and a wasteland.
\v 4 Your cities I will make a ruin, and you, you will be a desolation. And you will know that I am Yahweh.
\v 5 Because of there being to you an everlasting hostility, and you poured out the sons of Israel onto the hands of the sword in the time of their calamity, in the time of the iniquity of the end—
\v 6 therefore, {by} my life—the declaration of the Lord Yahweh—that I will make you for blood, and blood will pursue you. If you did not hate blood, but blood will pursue you.
\v 7 And I will make Mount Seir a desolation and a desolation, and I will cut off from it the one crossing over and the one returning.
\v 8 And I will fill his mountains with his slain ones. Your hills and your valleys and all your streams—the slain of the sword will fall in them.
\v 9 Everlasting desolations I will make you, and your cities will not be inhabited. \f + \ft The written text has \fqa will not be inhabited\fqa*; the reading tradition has \fqa will not return\fqa*.\f* And you will know that I am Yahweh.
\v 10 Because of your saying, “The two nations and the two lands, to me they will belong, and we will possess it,” and Yahweh was there—
\v 11 therefore, {by} my life—the declaration of the Lord Yahweh—I will act according to your nose and according to your jealousy that you did out of your hatreds against them. And I will make myself known among them just as I judge you.
\v 12 And you will know that I {am} Yahweh. I have heard all your blasphemies that you said against the mountains of Israel, saying, “They are desolate; to us they have been given for food.”
\v 13 And you magnified {yourselves} against me with your mouth, and you multiplied your words against me. I, I have heard.
\p
\v 14 Thus says the Lord Yahweh: Like the rejoicing of all the earth, a desolation I will make for you.
\v 15 Like your rejoicing over the inheritance of the house of Israel because it was desolate, thus I will do to you. A desolation you will be, Mount Seir, and all Edom, all of it. And they will know that I {am} Yahweh.’”
\c 36
\p
\v 1 “And you, son of man, prophesy to the mountains of Israel, and you shall say, ‘Mountains of Israel, hear the word of Yahweh!
\v 2 Thus says the Lord Yahweh: Because the enemy has said against you, “Aha!” and, “The eternal high places have become to us as a possession,”’
\v 3 therefore prophesy and you shall say, ‘Thus says the Lord Yahweh: Because, indeed because, of desolating and panting for you from all around, for your being a possession to the remnant of the nations, and you were taken up on the lip of the tongue and the evil report of a people,
\v 4 therefore, mountains of Israel, hear the word of the Lord Yahweh! Thus says the Lord Yahweh to the mountains and to the hills, to the streams and to the valleys, and to the desolate ruins and to the forsaken cities that have become plunder and scorn to the remnant of the nations that are all around—
\v 5 therefore thus says the Lord Yahweh: If not in the fire of my jealousy I have spoken against the remnant of the nations and against Edom, all of it, who gave my land to themselves as a possession with the joy of all the heart, with contempt in the soul, for the sake of its pastureland, for plunder.’
\v 6 Therefore prophesy concerning the land of Israel and you shall say to the mountains and to the hills, to the streams and to the valleys, ‘Thus says the Lord Yahweh: Behold me, in my jealousy and in my wrath I have spoken, because you have borne the humiliation of nations.
\v 7 Therefore thus says the Lord Yahweh: I, I have lifted up my hand—if not the nations that are around you, they, they will bear their humiliation.
\p
\v 8 But you, mountains of Israel, you will give your branch, and you will bear your fruit for my people Israel, for they have drawn near to come.
\v 9 For behold me for you, and I will turn to you, and you will be worked and you will be sown.
\v 10 And I will multiply man on you, all the house of Israel, all of it. And the cities will be inhabited, and the ruins will be built.
\v 11 And I will multiply on you man and beast, and they will multiply and be fruitful. And I will cause you to dwell as in your former times, and I will do good more than in your beginnings. And you will know that I am Yahweh.
\v 12 And I will cause man to walk on you, my people Israel, and they will possess you, and you will be to them as an inheritance, and you will not repeat again to be bereaved of them.
\v 13 Thus says the Lord Yahweh: Because they are saying to you, “A devourer of man you are, and a bereaved one of your nation you have been,”
\v 14 therefore man you will not devour again, and your nation you will not cause to stumble again— the declaration of the Lord Yahweh.
\v 15 And I will not cause you to hear the insult of the nations again, and the reproach of the peoples you will not bear again, and your nation you will not cause to stumble again— the declaration of the Lord Yahweh.’”
\p
\v 16 And the word of Yahweh was to me, saying,
\v 17 “Son of man, the house of Israel was dwelling on their ground, and they defiled it with their way and with their actions. Like the uncleanness of menstruation was their way to my face.
\v 18 And I poured out my wrath on them because of the blood that they poured out on the land, and with their idols they defiled it.
\v 19 And I scattered them among the nations, and they were dispersed among the lands. According to their way and according to their actions I judged them.
\v 20 And he came to the nations which they came there, and they profaned the name of my holiness, when to say of them, ‘These {are} the people of Yahweh, but from his land they went out.’
\v 21 And I had compassion on the name of my holiness, which the house of Israel profaned it among the nations which they came to there.
\p
\v 22 Therefore say to the house of Israel, ‘Thus says the Lord Yahweh: Not for your sake am I acting, house of Israel, but rather for the name of my holiness, which you profaned among the nations which you came there.
\v 23 And I will sanctify my great name, the one profaned among the nations, which you profaned in their midst. And the nations will know that I {am} Yahweh—the declaration of the Lord Yahweh—when I am sanctified through you to their eyes.
\v 24 And I will take you from the nations, and I will gather you from all the lands, and I will bring you to your ground.
\v 25 And I will sprinkle on you clean water, and you will be clean from all your uncleannesses, and from all your idols I will cleanse you.
\v 26 And I will give to you a new heart, and a new spirit I will put in your inward part. And I will remove the heart of stone from your flesh, and I will give to you a heart of flesh.
\v 27 And my Spirit I will put in your inward part, and I will do that which in my statutes you will walk, and my judgments you will keep and do.
\v 28 And you will dwell in the land that I gave to your fathers, and you will be to me as a people, and I, I will be to you as God.
\v 29 And I will save you from all your uncleannesses, and I will call to the grain and I will multiply it, and I will not put famine on you.
\v 30 And I will multiply the fruit of the tree and the produce of the field, so that you will not receive again the reproach of famine among the nations.
\v 31 And you will remember your evil ways and your actions that {were} not good, and you will feel loathing in your faces because of your iniquities and because of your abominations.
\p
\v 32 Not for your sake am I acting— the declaration of the Lord Yahweh— may it be known to you. Be ashamed and be humiliated because of your ways, house of Israel!
\v 33 Thus says the Lord Yahweh: On the day of my cleansing you from all of your iniquities, then I will cause the cities to be inhabited, and the ruins will be built.
\v 34 And the desolated land will be worked, in place of which it was a desolation to the eyes of everyone passing by.
\v 35 And they will say, “This here desolated land has become like the garden of Eden, and the ruined and the desolated and the torn-down cities {are} fortified; they are inhabited.”
\v 36 And the nations that are left around you will know that I, Yahweh, have built the torn-down {places}; I have planted the desolated {place}. I, Yahweh, have spoken, and I will do {it}.
\p
\v 37 Thus says the Lord Yahweh: Again for this I will be inquired of by the house of Israel, to do for them: I will multiply them like a flock of man.
\v 38 Like a flock of holy {ones}, like the flock of Jerusalem at her appointed times, thus the ruined cities will be full of a flock of man. And they will know that I {am} Yahweh.’”
\c 37
\p
\v 1 The hand of Yahweh was upon me, and he brought me out by the Spirit of Yahweh and placed me in the midst of the valley, and it {was} full of bones.
\v 2 And he made me pass over them around, around, and behold, {they were} very many upon the face of the valley, and behold, they {were} very dry.
\v 3 And he said to me, “Son of man, can these bones live?” And I said, “Lord Yahweh, you, you know.”
\v 4 And he said to me, “Prophesy over these bones, and you shall say to them, ‘O dry bones, hear the word of Yahweh!’
\v 5 Thus says the Lord Yahweh to these bones, ‘Behold, I am bringing breath into you, and you will live.
\v 6 And I will put sinews upon you, and I will bring up flesh upon you, and I will spread skin over you, and I will put breath in you, and you will live. And you will know that I {am} Yahweh.’”
\p
\v 7 And I prophesied just as I was commanded. And there was a sound as I prophesied, and behold, a rattling! And the bones drew near, bone to its bone.
\v 8 And I looked, and behold, sinews {were} upon them, and flesh came up, and skin spread over them from above, but there was no breath in them.
\v 9 And he said to me, “Prophesy to the breath! Prophesy, son of man, and you shall say to the breath, ‘Thus says the Lord Yahweh, “From the four winds come, O breath, and breathe into these killed ones, so that they may live.”’”
\v 10 And I prophesied just as he had commanded me, and the breath came into them, and they lived and stood upon their feet, a very, very great force.
\p
\v 11 And he said to me, “Son of man, these bones, they {are} all the house of Israel. Behold, they are saying, ‘Our bones have dried up, and our hope has perished. We are cut off to ourselves.’
\v 12 Therefore prophesy and say to them, ‘Thus says the Lord Yahweh, “Behold, I {am} opening your graves, and I will bring you up from your graves, my people, and I will bring you to the soil of Israel.
\v 13 And you will know that I am Yahweh when I open your graves and when I bring you up from your graves, my people.
\v 14 And I will put my Spirit in you, and you will live, and I will set you upon your soil. And you will know that I, Yahweh, I have spoken and I have done {it}”’”— the declaration of Yahweh.
\p
\v 15 And the word of Yahweh was to me, saying,
\v 16 “And you, son of man, take for yourself one wood and write on it, ‘For Judah and for the sons of Israel, his companion.’ And take one wood and write on it, ‘For Joseph, the wood of Ephraim, and all the house of Israel, his companion.’
\v 17 And bring them near, one to one, for yourself, into one wood, and they will be as ones in your hand.
\v 18 And when the sons of your people say to you, saying, ‘Will you not tell to us what these {are} to you?’
\v 19 speak to them, ‘Thus says the Lord Yahweh: “Behold, I am taking the wood of Joseph, which is in the hand of Ephraim, and the tribes of Israel, his companion, and I will put them upon it, with the wood of Judah, and I will make them into one wood, and they will be one in my hand.”’
\v 20 And the woods which you will write on them will be in your hand before their eyes.
\p
\v 21 And speak to them, ‘Thus says the Lord Yahweh, “Behold, I am taking the sons of Israel from among the nations where they have gone there, and I will gather them from all around, and I will bring them to their soil.
\v 22 And I will make them into one nation in the land, on the mountains of Israel, and one king will be for all of them as king. And they will no longer be two nations, and they will no longer be divided into two kingdoms again.
\v 23 And they will no longer defile themselves with their idols and with their abominations and with all their transgressions. And I will save them from all their dwelling places which they have sinned in them, and I will cleanse them. And they will be to me as a people, and I, I will be to them as God.
\p
\v 24 And my servant David {will be} king over them, and one shepherd will be for all of them. And they will walk in my judgments, and my statutes they will keep and do them.
\v 25 And they will dwell upon the land that I gave to my servant, to Jacob, which your fathers dwelt in it. And they will dwell upon it, they and their sons and the sons of their sons, forever. And David my servant will be prince to them forever.
\v 26 And I will cut for them a covenant of peace; it will be an everlasting covenant with them. And I will place them and I will multiply them, and I will put my sanctuary in their midst forever.
\v 27 And my dwelling place will be over them, and I will be to them as God, and they, they will be to me as a people.
\v 28 And the nations will know that I {am} Yahweh, {the one} sanctifying Israel, when my sanctuary is in their midst forever.”’”
\c 38
\p
\v 1 And the word of Yahweh was to me, saying,
\v 2 “Son of man, set your face toward Gog, the land of Magog, the chief prince of Meshech and Tubal, and prophesy against him,
\v 3 and you shall say, ‘Thus says the Lord Yahweh: Behold me against you, Gog, chief prince of Meshech and Tubal!
\v 4 And I will turn you back and put hooks in your jaws, and I will bring you out and all your army, horses and horsemen, all of them clothed in perfection, a large assembly {with} body shield and arm shield, all of them wielding swords.
\v 5 Persia, Cush, and Put {are} with them, all of them {with} shield and helmet.
\v 6 Gomer and all of its troops, Beth Togarmah {from} the recesses of the north and all of its troops—many peoples {are} with you.
\v 7 Be prepared, and prepare for yourself, you and all your assembly, the ones assembled to you, and you shall be to them as a guard.
\v 8 After many days you will be mustered. In the end of the years you will come to a land brought back from the sword, gathered from many peoples, upon the mountains of Israel, which had been for a ruin continually. But it, it will have been brought out from the peoples, and they will be dwelling in security, all of them.
\v 9 And you shall go up; like the storm you shall come. Like a cloud to cover the land you shall be, you and all of your troops and many peoples with you.
\p
\v 10 Thus says the Lord Yahweh: And it will happen on that day, words will come up on your heart, and you will scheme an evil scheme.
\v 11 And you will say, “I will go up against a land of open areas; I will come to the quiet ones, the dwellers in security, all of them dwelling without a wall, and bars and doors {are} not to them,
\v 12 to spoil spoil and to plunder plunder, to turn back your hand against the inhabited ruins and against a people gathered from the nations, making livestock and property, the dwellers upon the center of the earth.”
\v 13 Sheba and Dedan and the merchants of Tarshish and all of its young lions will say to you, “Is it to spoil spoil that you are coming? Is it to plunder plunder that you have assembled your assembly, to carry silver and gold, to take livestock and property, to spoil a great spoil?”’
\p
\v 14 Therefore prophesy, son of man, and you shall say to Gog, ‘Thus says the Lord Yahweh: Will you not know on that day, when my people Israel are dwelling in security?
\v 15 And you will come from your place, from the recesses of the north, you and many peoples with you, all of them riders of horses, a great assembly and a large army.
\v 16 And you will go up against my people Israel like a cloud to cover the land. In the end of the days it will be, and I will bring you against my land, in order for the nations to know me when I am sanctified through you to their eyes, Gog.
\p
\v 17 Thus says the Lord Yahweh: Are you he {about} whom I spoke in former days by the hand of my servants the prophets of Israel, the ones prophesying in those days {for} years, to bring you against them?
\v 18 But it will happen on that day, on the day of the coming of Gog onto the soil of Israel—the declaration of the Lord Yahweh—my fury will go up in my nose.
\v 19 And in my jealousy, in the fire of my wrath, I have spoken: If there will not be on that day a great earthquake upon the soil of Israel.
\v 20 And the fish of the sea and the bird of the heavens and the living thing of the field and every creeping thing creeping upon the ground and every man who is upon the face of the ground will quake from my face. And the mountains will be thrown down, and the steep places will fall, and every wall will fall to the ground.
\v 21 And I will call a sword against him on all my mountains—the declaration of the Lord Yahweh—the sword of a man will be against his brother.
\v 22 And I will enter into judgment with him with plague and with blood. And overflowing rain and stones of hail, fire and sulfur, I will rain upon him and upon his troops and upon the many peoples who are with him.
\v 23 And I will magnify myself and I will sanctify myself, and I will be known to the eyes of many nations. And they will know that I am Yahweh.’”
\c 39
\p
\v 1 “And you, son of man, prophesy against Gog and you shall say, ‘Thus says the Lord Yahweh: Behold me against you, Gog, chief prince of Meshech and Tubal!
\v 2 And I will turn you back and lead you on, and I will bring you up from the recesses of the north, and I will bring you onto the mountains of Israel.
\v 3 And I will strike your bow from your left hand, and I will make your arrows fall from your right hand.
\v 4 On the mountains of Israel you will fall, you and all of your troops and the peoples who are with you. To the raptor, the bird of every wing, and to the living thing of the field I have given you as food.
\v 5 On the face of the field you will fall, for I, I have spoken—the declaration of the Lord Yahweh.
\v 6 And I will send fire against Magog and against the dwellers of the coastlands in security. And they will know that I am Yahweh.
\v 7 And the name of my holiness I will make known in the midst of my people Israel, and I will not allow the name of my holiness to be profaned again. And the nations will know that I am Yahweh, holy in Israel.
\v 8 Behold, it is coming and it will be done—the declaration of the Lord Yahweh. It is the day which I have promised.
\v 9 And the dwellers of the cities of Israel will go out, and they will kindle and set fire to the weaponry and arm shield and body shield, to bow and to arrows and to staff of hand and to spear. And they will kindle fire with them seven years.
\v 10 And they will not carry woods from the field, and they will not chop {wood} from the forests, for with the weaponry they will kindle fire. And they will spoil their spoilers and plunder their plunderers— the declaration of the Lord Yahweh.
\p
\v 11 And it will happen on that day, I will give to Gog a place there, a grave in Israel, the Valley of the Travelers, east of the sea. And it, it is blocking the travelers. And there they will bury Gog and all of his multitude, and they will call {it} the Valley of Hamon Gog.
\v 12 And the house of Israel will bury them in order to cleanse the land, seven months.
\v 13 And all of the people of the land will bury {them}, and it will be to them for a name, the day of my being glorified—the declaration of the Lord Yahweh.
\v 14 And they will set apart men of continuance, ones passing through in the land, burying the travelers, the ones remaining on the face of the land, to cleanse it. From the end of seven months they will search.
\v 15 And the travelers will pass through in the land, and one will see a bone of a man and build a marker beside it, until the ones burying have buried it in the Valley of Hamon Gog.’
\v 16 (And also Hamonah {is} the name of a city.) ‘And they will cleanse the land.’
\p
\v 17 And you, son of man, thus says the Lord Yahweh: Say to the bird of every wing and to every living thing of the field, ‘Be gathered and come; be assembled from all around to my sacrifice that I am sacrificing for you, a great sacrifice on the mountains of Israel. And you shall eat flesh and shall drink blood.
\v 18 The flesh of warriors you will eat, and the blood of the princes of the earth you will drink— rams, lambs, and male goats, bulls, fatlings of Bashan, all of them.
\v 19 And you will eat fat to satiety, and you will drink blood to drunkenness, from my sacrifice that I will have sacrificed for you.
\v 20 And you will be satisfied at my table {with} horse and rider, warrior and every man of war— the declaration of the Lord Yahweh.’
\v 21 And I will set my glory among the nations, and all the nations will see my justice that I have done and my hand that I have placed on them.
\v 22 And the house of Israel will know that I am Yahweh their God from that day and beyond.
\v 23 And the nations will know that the house of Israel went into exile for their iniquity, because they acted unfaithfully against me. And I hid my face from them and gave them into the hand of their adversaries, and all of them fell by the sword.
\v 24 According to their uncleanness and according to their transgressions I did to them, and I hid my face from them.
\p
\v 25 Therefore thus says the Lord Yahweh: Now I will restore the fortunes of Jacob, and I will have compassion on all of the house of Israel, and I will be jealous for the name of my holiness.
\v 26 And they will bear their humiliation and all of their unfaithfulness that they acted unfaithfully against me, when they are dwelling on their soil in security and there is no one making {them} afraid.
\v 27 In my bringing them back from the peoples—and I will gather them from the lands of their enemies—then I will be sanctified in them before the eyes of many nations.
\v 28 And they will know that I am Yahweh their God, in my exiling them to the nations, and I will gather them to their soil. And I will not leave any of them there again.
\v 29 And I will not hide my face from them again when I have poured out my Spirit on the house of Israel— the declaration of the Lord Yahweh.”
\c 40
\p
\v 1 In year 25 of our exile in the head of the year on the tenth of the month, in year 14 after the city was struck, on this same day, the hand of Yahweh was upon me and he brought me there.
\v 2 In visions of God he brought me to the land of Israel, and he made me rest to a very high mountain, and upon it from the south {was} like a structure of a city.
\v 3 And he brought me there, and behold, a man! His appearance {was} like the appearance of bronze, and a cord of linen {was} in his hand and the reed of the measurement, and he was standing in the gate.
\v 4 And the man spoke to me, “Son of man, see with your eyes, and with your ears hear, and set your heart to all that I am making you see, for in order to make you see you were brought here. Declare all that you are seeing to the house of Israel.”
\p
\v 5 And behold, a wall from outside to the house around, around. And in the hand of the man the reed of the measurement {was} six cubits in the cubit and a handbreadth. And he measured the width of the structure, one reed, and the height, one reed.
\v 6 And he went to a gate whose face {was} the way to the east, and he went up its steps. And he measured the sill of the gate\f + \ft After \fqa one stick in depth\fqa*, the Hebrew text reads in addition: \fqa one threshold one stick in depth”\fqa*. Many modern versions, however, leave this expression out, because it seems to be a repetition of preceding text.\f* , one reed {in} width, and one sill, one reed {in} width.
\v 7 And the recess {was} one reed {in} length and one reed {in} width, and between the recesses {were} five cubits. And the sill of the gate from beside the porch of the gate from the house {was} one reed.
\v 8 And he measured the porch of the gate from the house, one reed.
\v 9 And he measured the porch of the gate, eight cubits, and its jamb {was} two cubits, and the porch of the gate {was} from the house.
\v 10 And the recesses of the gate, the way of the east, {were} three from here and three from there, one measurement for their three, and one measurement for the jambs from here and from there.
\v 11 And he measured the width of the opening of the gate, ten cubits. The length of the gate: thirteen cubits.
\v 12 And a border to the face of the recesses, one cubit, and one cubit a border from here. And the recess, six cubits from here and six cubits from there.
\v 13 And he measured the gate from the roof of the recess to its roof, {in} width 25 cubits, an opening in front of an opening.
\v 14 And he did the jambs, 60 cubits, and to the jamb of the courtyard, the gate around, around.
\v 15 And on the face of the gate of the entrance on to the face of the porch of the inner gate, 50 cubits.
\v 16 And shut windows {were} to the recesses and to their jambs, to the inside to the gate around, around, and thus for the porches. And windows {were} around, around to the inside, and to a jam {were} palm trees.
\p
\v 17 And he brought me to the outer courtyard, and behold, chambers and a pavement, made for the courtyard around, around. Thirty chambers {were} toward the pavement.
\v 18 And the pavement {was} to the shoulder of the gates, corresponding to the length of the gates: the lower pavement.
\v 19 And he measured the width from the face of the lower gate to the face of the inner courtyard from outside, 100 cubits, the east and the north.
\p
\v 20 And the gate whose face {was} the way of the north, to the outer courtyard, he measured its length and its width.
\v 21 And its recess, three from here and three from there, and its jamb and its porch were according to the measurement of the first gate: 50 cubits its length, and width 25 in the cubit.
\v 22 And its window and its porch and its palm tree {were} according to the measurement of the gate whose face {was} the way of the east. And by seven steps they would go up on it, and its porch {was} to their face.
\v 23 And a gate for the inner courtyard {was} in front of the gate to the north and to the east. And he measured from a gate to a gate, 100 cubits.
\p
\v 24 And he led me the way of the south, and behold, the gate of the way of the south. And he measured its jamb and its porch according to these measurements.
\v 25 And windows {were} for it and for its porch around, around, according to these windows, 50 cubits {in} length, and {in} width 25 cubits.
\v 26 And seven steps {were} its goings up, and its porch {was} to their face; and palm trees {were} for it, one from here and one from there, to its jamb.
\v 27 And a gate to the inner courtyard {was} the way of the south. And he measured from a gate to the gate, the way of the south, 100 cubits.
\p
\v 28 And he brought me to the inner courtyard by the gate of the south. And he measured the gate of the south according to these measurements.
\v 29 And its recess and its jamb and its porch {were} according to these measurements, and windows for it and for its porch around, around, 50 cubits {in} length, and {in} width 25 cubits.
\v 30 And porches {were} around, around, {in} length 25 cubits and {in} width five cubits.
\v 31 And its porch {was} to the outer courtyard, and palm trees {were} to its jamb, and eight steps {were} its ascent.
\p
\v 32 And he brought me to the inner courtyard, the way of the east, and he measured the gate according to these measurements.
\v 33 And its recess and its jamb and its porch {were} according to these measurements, and windows for it and for its porch around, around, {in} length 50 cubits, and {in} width 25 cubits.
\v 34 And its porch {was} to the outer courtyard, and palm trees {were} to its jamb from here and from there, and eight steps {were} its ascent.
\p
\v 35 And he brought me to the gate of the north, and he measured according to these measurements,
\v 36 its recess, its jamb, and its porch, and windows for it around, around, {in} length 50 cubits, and {in} width 25 cubits.
\v 37 And its jamb {was} to the outer courtyard, and palm trees {were} to its jamb from here and from there, and eight steps {were} its ascent.
\p
\v 38 And a chamber and its opening {were} by the jambs of the gates; there they rinse the burnt offering.
\v 39 And in the porch of the gate {were} two tables from here and two tables from there, to slaughter to them the burnt offering and the sin offering and the guilt offering.
\v 40 And to the shoulder from to the outside for the one going up to the opening of the gate to the north {were} two tables; and to the other shoulder that {was} for the porch of the gate {were} two tables.
\v 41 Four tables from here and four tables from there to the shoulder of the gate, eight tables, to them they slaughter.
\v 42 And four tables for the burnt offering {were} stones of hewn stone, {in} length one cubit and a half, and {in} width one cubit and a half, and {in} height one cubit. To them, and they made rest the vessels with which they slaughter the burnt offering and the sacrifice.
\v 43 And the hooks, one handbreadth, {were} established in the house around, around, and to the tables {was} the flesh of the offering.
\p
\v 44 And from to the outside of the inner gate {were} chambers of singers in the inner courtyard, which {were} to the shoulder of the gate of the north, and their faces {were} the way of the south. One {was} to the shoulder of the gate of the east, the face of the way of the north.
\v 45 And he spoke to me, “This {is} the chamber, whose face {is} the way of the south, for the priests, the ones keeping the keeping of the house.
\v 46 And the chamber whose face {is} the way of the north {is} for the priests, the ones keeping the keeping of the altar. They {are} the sons of Zadok, the ones coming near from the sons of Levi to Yahweh, to minister to him.”
\v 47 And he measured the courtyard, {in} length 100 cubits, and {in} width 100 cubits, square. And the altar {was} to the face of the house.
\p
\v 48 And he brought me to the porch of the house, and he measured a jamb of a porch, five cubits from here and five cubits from there. And the width of the gate {was} three cubits from here and three cubits from there.
\v 49 The length of the porch {was} 20 cubits, and {in} width 11 cubits, and by the steps {by} which they would go up to it. And pillars {were} to the jambs, one from here and one from there.
\c 41
\p
\v 1 And he brought me to the nave, and he measured the jambs, six cubits {in} width from here and six cubits {in} width from there, the width of the tent.
\v 2 And the width of the entrance {was} ten cubits, and the shoulders of the opening {were} five cubits from here and five cubits from there. And he measured its length, 40 cubits, and {in} width, 20 cubits.
\v 3 And he went to the inside, and he measured the jamb of the opening, two cubits, and the opening, six cubits, and the width of the opening, seven cubits.
\v 4 And he measured its length, 20 cubits, and {in} width, 20 cubits, to the face of the nave. And he said to me, “This {is} the Holy of Holies.”
\p
\v 5 And he measured the wall of the house, six cubits, and the width of the side chamber, four cubits around, around the house, around.
\v 6 And the side chambers {were} a side chamber to a side chamber, 33 times, and going in the wall that {was} for the house, for the side rooms around, around, to be held. And they were not held in the wall of the house.
\v 7 And it widened and turned to above, to above for the side chambers, for the turning of the house {was} to above, to above around, around for the house. Therefore, width for the house {was} to above. And thus he goes up the lower upon the highest to the middle.
\v 8 And I saw for the house a height around, around. The founded things of the side chambers {were} the fullness of the reed, six cubits, a joint.
\v 9 The width of the wall that {was} for the side chamber to the outside {was} five cubits. And what was made rest {was} a house of side rooms that {was} to the house,
\v 10 and between the chambers {was} a width of 20 cubits around to the house, around, around.
\v 11 And the opening of the side chamber {was} to the thing being made rest. One opening {was} the way of the north, and one opening {was} to the south. And the width of the place of the thing being made rest {was} five cubits around, around.
\p
\v 12 And the structure that {was} to the face of the court, the side of the way of the sea, {was} a width of 70 cubits. And the wall of the structure {was} five cubits {in} width around, around, and its length {was} 90 cubits.
\v 13 And he measured the house, {in} length 100 cubits. And the court and the structure and its walls, {in} length 100 cubits.
\v 14 And the width of the face of the house and the court to the east {was} 100 cubits.
\v 15 And he measured the length of the structure to the face of the court that {was} behind it, and its ledges from here and from there, 100 cubits.
\p And the nave, the inner, and the porches of the courtyard,
\v 16 the sills and the shut windows and the ledges around for the three of them, in front of the sill, {were} paneled of wood around, around, and the ground up to the windows (and the windows {were} being covered),
\v 17 upon from upon the opening and up to the inner house and to the outside and to all the wall around, around, on the inner and on the outer, measurements.
\v 18 And {it was} made {with} cherubs and palm trees, and a palm tree between cherub to cherub, and two faces {were} to the cherub.
\v 19 And the face of a man {was} to the palm tree from here, and the face of a young lion {was} to the palm tree from there. {It was} made to all the house around, around.
\v 20 From the ground up to from upon the opening the cherubs and the palm trees were made, and the wall of the nave.
\p
\v 21 The nave, the doorpost {was} square. And the face of the holy place, the appearance {was} according to the appearance.
\v 22 The altar, wood, {was} three cubits high, and its length {was} two cubits. And its corners to it and its length and its walls {were} wood. And he spoke to me, “This {is} the table that {is} to the face of Yahweh.”
\v 23 And two doors {were} for the nave and for the holy place.
\v 24 And two doors {were} for the doors, two turning doors: two for one door and two doors for the other.
\v 25 And made to them, to the doors of the nave, {were} cherubs and palm trees, just as {were} made for the walls. And a roof of wood {was} to the face of the porch from the outside.
\v 26 And shut windows and palm trees {were} from here and from there, to the shoulders of the porch, and the side chambers of the house and the roofs.
\c 42
\p
\v 1 And he brought me out to the outer courtyard, the way, the way of the north. And he brought me to the chamber that {was} in front of the court and that {was} in front of the structure to the north.
\v 2 To the face of the length, 100 cubits, {was} the opening of the north, and the width, 50 cubits.
\v 3 In front of the 20 that {were} for the inner courtyard, and in front of the pavement that {was} for the outer courtyard, {was} a ledge to a face of a ledge in the third.
\v 4 And to the face of the chambers {was} a passage of ten cubits {in} width to the inner, a way of one cubit; and their openings {were} to the north.
\v 5 And the highest chambers {were} shorter, for ledges ate from them, from the lowers and from the middles of the structure.
\v 6 For they {were} made three, and there were not for them pillars like the pillars of the courtyards. Therefore it was withdrawn from the lowers and from the middles, from the ground.
\v 7 And a wall that {was} to the outside, corresponding to the chambers, the way of the outer courtyard to the face of the chambers, its length {was} 50 cubits.
\v 8 For the length of the chambers that {were} for the outer courtyard {was} 50 cubits, and behold, upon the face of the nave {was} 100 cubits.
\v 9 And from under these chambers {was} the entrance from the east, in his going to them from the outer courtyard,
\v 10 in the width of the wall of the courtyard.
\p The way of the east, to the face of the court and to the face of the structure, {were} chambers.
\v 11 And a way {was} to their faces, according to the appearance of the chambers that {were} the way of the north. According to their length, thus their width; and all of their goings out, and according to their ordinances and according to their openings.
\v 12 And according to the openings of the chambers that {were} the way of the south {was} an opening at a head of a way, a way in the face of the protecting wall, the way of the east in their going.
\p
\v 13 And he said to me, “The chambers of the north, the chambers of the south, which {are} to the face of the court, they {are} the chambers of the holy place, where the priests who {are} near to Yahweh eat the holy things of the holy things. There they make rest the holy things of the holy things and the grain offering and the sin offering and the guilt offering, for the place {is} holy.
\v 14 In their going, the priests, they do not go out from the holy place to the outer courtyard, and there they make rest their clothes in which they minister, for they {are} holy. They put on other clothes, and they come near to what {is} for the people.”
\p
\v 15 And he finished the measurements of the inner house, and he brought me out the way of the gate whose face {was} the way of the east, and he measured it around, around.
\v 16 He measured the wind of the east with the reed of the measurement: five cubits, reeds, in the reed of the measurement around.
\v 17 He measured the wind of the north: 500, reeds, in the reed of the measurement around.
\v 18 The wind of the south he measured: 500, reeds, in the reed of the measurement.
\v 19 He turned to the wind of the sea. He measured 500, reeds, in the reed of the measurement.
\v 20 To four winds he measured it. A wall {was} for it around, around, {in} length 500 and {in} width 500, to separate between the holy to common.
\c 43
\p
\v 1 And he led me to the gate, a gate that is facing the way of the east.
\v 2 And behold, the glory of the God of Israel came from the way of the east, and his voice {was} like the voice of many waters, and the earth shone from his glory.
\v 3 And according to appearance, the appearance that I saw {was} like the appearance that I saw in my coming to destroy the city. And the appearances {were} like the appearance that I saw to the river of Kebar, and I fell to my face.
\v 4 And the glory of Yahweh came to the house {by} a way of a gate whose face {was} the way of the east.
\v 5 And a wind lifted me and brought me to the inner courtyard, and behold, the glory of Yahweh filled the house.
\p
\v 6 And I heard one speaking to me from the house, and a man was standing beside me.
\v 7 And he said to me, “Son of man, {this is} the place of my throne and the place of the soles of my feet, where I will dwell in the midst of the sons of Israel forever. And the house of Israel will not make the name of my holiness unclean again, they and their kings, with their prostitution and with the corpses of their kings {at} their high places,
\v 8 in their putting their sill with my sill and their doorpost beside my doorpost, and the wall between me and between them. And they made the name of my holiness unclean with their abominations that they did, and I finished them in my nose.
\v 9 Now let them put far away their prostitution and the corpses of their kings from me, and I will dwell in their midst forever.
\p
\v 10 You, son of man, declare {to} the house of Israel the house, and let them be humiliated from their iniquities, and let them measure the pattern.
\v 11 And if they are humiliated from all that they have done, the plan of the house and its arrangement and its goings out and its entrances and all its plans and all its statutes and all my plans and all its laws make known {to} them. And write to their eyes, and they shall keep all its plan and all its statutes, and they shall do them.
\v 12 This {is} the law of the house: upon the head of the mountain, all of its border around, around, {is} a holy of holies. Behold, this {is} the law of the house.
\p
\v 13 And these {are} the measurements of the altar in cubits (a cubit {is} a cubit and a handbreadth): and a bosom {is} the cubit, and a cubit {in} width, and its border to its lip around {is} one span. And this {is} the base of the altar:
\v 14 And from the bosom of the ground up to the lower setback {is} two cubits, and {in} width one cubit. And from the small setback up to the great setback {is} four cubits, and {in} width the cubit.
\v 15 And the hearth {is} four cubits, and from the hearth and upward, the horns {are} four.
\v 16 And the hearth {is} 12 {in} length by 12 {in} width, square to the four of its sides.
\v 17 And the setback {is} 14 {in} length by 14 {in} width to the four of its sides, and the border around it {is} the half of the cubit, and the bosom for it {is} a cubit around. And its steps to face east.”
\p
\v 18 And he said to me, “Son of man, thus says the Lord Yahweh: ‘These {are} the statutes of the altar on the day of its being made, to make a burnt offering go up on it and to splash blood on it.
\v 19 And you shall give to the priests, the Levites who {are} from the seed of Zadok, the ones near to me’—the declaration of the Lord Yahweh—‘to minister to me, a bull, a son of cattle, for a sin offering.
\v 20 And you shall take from its blood and put on its four horns and to the four corners of the setback and to the border around, and you shall purify it and make atonement for it.
\v 21 And you shall take the bull of the sin offering, and he shall burn it in the appointed place of the house, from outside to the holy place.
\v 22 And on the second day you shall present a buck of the goats, perfect, for a sin offering; and they shall purify the altar, just as they purified with the bull.
\v 23 In your finishing from purifying, you shall present a bull, a son of cattle, perfect, and a ram from the flock, perfect.
\v 24 And you shall present them to the face of Yahweh, and the priests shall throw salt on them, and they shall make them go up {as} a burnt offering to Yahweh.
\v 25 Seven days you shall do a buck of a sin offering for the day, and a bull, a son of cattle, and a ram from the flock, perfect, they shall do.
\v 26 Seven days they shall make atonement for the altar, and they shall cleanse it, and they shall fill its hand.
\v 27 And they shall finish the days. And it will be on the eighth day and beyond, the priests shall do upon the altar your burnt offerings and your peace offerings, and I will accept you’—the declaration of the Lord Yahweh.”
\c 44
\p
\v 1 And he returned me the way of the gate of the outer holy place, the one facing east, and it was being shut.
\v 2 And Yahweh said to me, “This gate shall be shut; it shall not be opened, and a man shall not come in it, for Yahweh, the God of Israel, came in it. And it shall be shut.
\v 3 The prince, he {is} a prince. He shall dwell in it to eat bread to the face of Yahweh. From the way of the porch of the gate he shall come, and from its way he shall go out.”
\p
\v 4 And he brought me the way of the gate of the north to the face of the house. And I saw, and behold, the glory of Yahweh filled the house of Yahweh, and I fell to my face.
\v 5 And Yahweh said to me, “Son of man, set your heart and see with your eyes and with your ears hear all that I am speaking {to} you, for all the statutes of the house of Yahweh and for all its laws. And you shall set your heart to the entrance of the house in all the goings out of the holy place.
\v 6 And you shall say to a rebellion, to the house of Israel, ‘Thus says the Lord Yahweh, “Great to you from all your abominations, house of Israel,
\v 7 in your bringing sons of a foreigner, uncircumcised ones of heart and uncircumcised ones of flesh, to be in my holy place, to profane it, my house, in your presenting my bread, fat and blood. And they broke my covenant to all your abominations.
\v 8 And you have not kept the keeping of my holy things, and you have put to ones keeping my keeping in my holy place for you.”
\p
\v 9 Thus says the Lord Yahweh, “Every son of a foreigner, an uncircumcised one of heart and an uncircumcised one of flesh, will not come to my holy place, for every son of a foreigner who {is} in the midst of the sons of Israel.
\v 10 But the Levites, who went far away from upon me in the going astray of Israel, who went astray from upon me after their idols, and they shall bear their iniquity.
\v 11 And they shall be ones ministering in my holy place, overseers to the gates of the house, and ones ministering to the house. They, they shall slaughter the burnt offering and the sacrifice for the people, and they, they shall stand to their face to minister to them.
\v 12 Because they served them to the face of their idols, and they were for the house of Israel for an obstacle of iniquity, therefore I have lifted up my hand against them”—the declaration of the Lord Yahweh—“and they shall bear their iniquity.
\v 13 And they shall not draw near to me to serve as a priest to me, nor to draw near to all of my holy things, to the holy things of the holy things. And they shall bear their humiliation and their abominations that they did.
\v 14 And I will make them keepers of the keeping of the house, for all of its service and for all that will be done in it.
\p
\v 15 But the priests, the Levites, the sons of Zadok, who kept the keeping of my sanctuary in the going astray of the sons of Israel from me, they, they shall draw near to me to serve me. And they shall stand to my face to present to me fat and blood—the declaration of the Lord Yahweh.
\v 16 They, they shall come to my sanctuary, and they, they shall draw near to my table to serve me, and they shall keep my keeping.
\v 17 And it will be, in their coming into the gates of the inner courtyard, they shall put on garments of linen; and wool shall not come up on them in their serving in the gates of the inner courtyard and toward the house.
\v 18 Headdresses of linen shall be on their head, and undergarments of linen shall be on their loins. They shall not gird themselves with sweat.
\v 19 And in their going out to the outer courtyard, to the outer courtyard to the people, they shall strip off their garments which they were serving in them and shall lay them in the chambers of the holiness. And they shall put on other garments, and they shall not make the people holy with their garments.
\v 20 And they shall not shave their head, and they shall not let {their} locks hang loose. Trimming they shall trim their heads.
\v 21 And every priest shall not drink wine in their coming into the inner courtyard.
\v 22 And a widow or a divorced {woman} they shall not take for themselves as wives, but rather virgins from the seed of the house of Israel. But the widow who is a widow from a priest they may take.
\v 23 And they shall teach my people between the holy and the common, and between the unclean and the clean they shall make them know.
\v 24 And over a dispute they, they shall stand to judge {it}; with my judgments they shall judge it. And they shall keep my laws and my statutes in all my appointed times, and they shall make my Sabbaths holy.
\v 25 And he shall not come to a dead man to become unclean; but rather for a father or for a mother or for a son or for a daughter, for a brother or for a sister who has not been to a man, they may make themselves unclean.
\v 26 And after his cleansing, seven days they shall count for him.
\v 27 And on the day of his coming to the Holy Place, to the inner courtyard, to serve in the Holy Place, he shall present his sin offering—the declaration of the Lord Yahweh.
\p
\v 28 And it shall be for them as an inheritance: I am their inheritance. And you shall not give them a possession in Israel; I am their possession.
\v 29 The grain offering and the sin offering and the guilt offering, they, they shall eat them. And every devoted thing in Israel shall be for them.
\v 30 And the first of all of the firstfruits of everything and every contribution of everything, from all of your contributions, shall be for the priests. And you shall give the first of your dough to the priest, to make a blessing rest on your house.
\v 31 Any carcass or torn {animal}, from the bird or from the beast, the priests shall not eat.’”
\c 45
\p
\v 1 And in your causing the land to fall as an inheritance, you shall offer up an offering to Yahweh, a holy thing from the land: a length of 25,000 in length, and a width of 10,000. It {is} holy\f + \ft Instead of \fqa 10,000\fqa*, which the Hebrew text has, some ancient versions have \fqa 20,000\fqa*.\f* in all its border all around.
\v 2 From this there will be for the Holy Place 500 by 500, squared all around, and 50 cubits of pastureland for it all around.
\v 3 And from this measurement you shall measure a length of 25,000 and a width of 10,000. And in it will be the sanctuary, the holy of holies.
\v 4 It {is} a holy thing from the land. It shall be for the priests, the ones serving the sanctuary, the ones near to serve Yahweh. And it shall be for them a place for houses and a sanctuary for the sanctuary.
\v 5 And 25,000 in length and 10,000 in width shall be for the Levites, the ones serving the house, for them as a possession: 20 chambers.
\v 6 And you shall give the possession of the city, 5,000 in width and 25,000 in length, corresponding to the contribution of the holiness. It shall be for all the house of Israel.
\v 7 And for the prince, from this and from this, for the contribution of the holiness and for the possession of the city, to the face of the contribution of the holiness and to the face of the possession of the city, from the side of the sea seaward and from the side of the east eastward. And the length {will be} corresponding to one of the portions, from the border of the sea to the border eastward.
\v 8 As for the land, it shall be for him as a possession in Israel. And my princes shall no longer mistreat my people, and they shall give the land to the house of Israel for their tribes.
\p
\v 9 Thus says the Lord Yahweh, “Enough for you, princes of Israel! Remove violence and destruction, and do justice and righteousness. Lift up your evictions from upon my people— the declaration of the Lord Yahweh.
\v 10 May scales of righteousness and an ephah of righteousness and a bath of righteousness be for you.
\v 11 The ephah and the bath shall be one quantity, to carry the tenth part of the homer, the bath, and the tenth of the homer, the ephah. To the homer shall be its proportion.
\v 12 And the shekel {is} 20 gerahs. Twenty shekels, 25 shekels, 15 shekels, the mina shall be for you.
\p
\v 13 This is the offering that you shall offer up: a sixth of the ephah from a homer of the wheat, and you shall give a sixth of the ephah from a homer of the barley.
\v 14 And the statute of the oil, the bath of the oil: the tenth part of the bath from the cor—ten baths{, that is,} a homer, for ten baths {are} a homer.
\v 15 And one sheep from the flock, from the 200, from the watering place of Israel—for a grain offering and for a burnt offering and for peace offerings, to make atonement for them—the declaration of the Lord Yahweh.
\v 16 All of the people of the land shall be for this contribution for the prince in Israel.
\v 17 And on the prince shall be the burnt offerings and the grain offering and the drink offering at the festivals and at the new moons and on the Sabbaths, at all the appointed times of the house of Israel. He, he will make the sin offering and the grain offering and the burnt offering and the peace offerings, to make atonement on behalf of the house of Israel.”
\p
\v 18 Thus says the Lord Yahweh, “In the first {month}, on the first of the month, you shall take a bull, a son of the cattle, perfect, and you shall purify the sanctuary.
\v 19 And the priest shall take from the blood of the sin offering and put {it} on the doorpost of the house and on the four corners of the ledge of the altar and on the doorpost of the gate of the inner courtyard.
\v 20 And thus you shall do on the seventh of the month on account of a man going astray and on account of a naive one, and you shall make atonement for the house.
\p
\v 21 In the first {month}, on the fourteenth day of the month, the Passover shall be for you, a festival of weeks of days; unleavened bread will be eaten.\f + \ft Instead of \fqa weeks\fqa*, which the Hebrew text has, some ancient versions have \fqa seven\fqa*, that is, “a festival of seven days.”\f*
\v 22 And on that day the prince shall make on behalf of himself and on behalf of all of the people of the land a bull of a sin offering.
\v 23 And the seven days of the festival he shall make a burnt offering to Yahweh, seven bulls and seven rams, perfect ones, for the day, seven of the days; and a sin offering, a buck of the goats for the day.
\v 24 And he shall make a grain offering, an ephah for the bull and an ephah for the ram, and oil, a hin for the ephah.
\v 25 In the seventh {month}, on the fifteenth day of the month, at the festival, he shall make like these the seven days, like the sin offering, like the burnt offering, and like the grain offering, and like the oil.”
\c 46
\p
\v 1 Thus says the Lord Yahweh: “The gate of the inner courtyard, the {one}facing east, shall be shut the six days of the work, and on the day of the Sabbath it shall be opened, and on the day of the new moon it shall be opened.
\v 2 And the prince shall come in {by} the way of the porch of the gate from outside, and he shall stand at the doorpost of the gate. And the priests shall make his burnt offering and his peace offerings, and he shall bow down at the threshold of the gate. And he shall go out, and the gate shall not be shut until the evening.
\v 3 And the people of the land shall bow down at the entrance of that gate on the Sabbaths and on the new moons to the face of Yahweh.
\v 4 And the burnt offering that the prince shall present to Yahweh on the day of the Sabbath: six lambs, perfect, and a ram, perfect.
\v 5 And a grain offering: an ephah for the ram; and for the lambs, a grain offering, the gift of his hand; and oil, a hin for the ephah.
\p
\v 6 And on the day of the new moon: a bull, a son of the perfect cattle, and six lambs and a ram; they shall be perfect.
\v 7 And an ephah for the bull and an ephah for the ram he shall make {as} a grain offering, and for the lambs just as his hand reaches; and oil, a hin for the ephah.
\v 8 And in the coming of the prince, {by} the way of the porch of the gate he shall come in, and by its way he shall go out.
\p
\v 9 And in the coming of the people of the land to the face of Yahweh at the appointed times, the one coming in {by} the way of the gate of the north to bow down shall go out {by} the way of the gate of the south, and the one coming in {by} the way of the gate of the south shall go out {by} the way of the gate northward. He shall not return {by} the way of the gate that he came in by it, for in front of him they shall go out.
\v 10 And the prince {shall be} in their midst; in their coming in he shall come in, and in their going out they shall go out.
\v 11 And at the festivals and at the appointed times the grain offering shall be an ephah for the bull and an ephah for the ram, and for the lambs the gift of his hand; and oil, a hin for the ephah.
\p
\v 12 And when the prince makes a freewill offering, a burnt offering or peace offerings, a freewill offering to Yahweh, then {someone} shall open for him the gate facing east, and he shall make his burnt offering and his peace offerings just as he does on the day of the Sabbath. Then he shall go out, and {someone} shall shut the gate after his going out.
\v 13 And a lamb, a son of its year, perfect, you shall make {as} a burnt offering for the day to Yahweh; in the morning, in the morning you shall make it.
\v 14 And a grain offering you shall make on it in the morning, in the morning: a sixth of the ephah, and oil, a third of the hin, to moisten the fine flour—a grain offering to Yahweh, {as} enduring statutes, continually.
\v 15 And they shall make the lamb and the grain offering and the oil in the morning, in the morning, a burnt offering of continuance.”
\p
\v 16 Thus says the Lord Yahweh: “When the prince gives a gift to a man from his sons, it {is} his inheritance. It shall be for his sons; it is their possession by inheritance.
\v 17 But when he gives a gift from his inheritance to one from his servants, then it shall be for him until the year of the liberty, and it shall return to the prince. Only his inheritance—his sons—for them it shall be.
\v 18 And the prince shall not take from the inheritance of the people, to mistreat them from their possession. From his possession he shall cause his sons to inherit, so that my people shall not scatter, a man from his possession.”
\p
\v 19 And he brought me in the entrance that {was} at the shoulder of the gate, to the chambers of the holiness, to the priests, the ones facing northward. And behold, a place was there in their recesses seaward.
\v 20 And he said to me, “This is the place where the priests shall boil there the guilt offering and the sin offering, where they shall bake the grain offering, so as not to bring {them} out to the outer courtyard, to make the people holy.”
\v 21 And he brought me out to the outer courtyard and made me pass over to the four corners of the courtyard. And behold, a courtyard {was} in a corner of the courtyard, a courtyard in a corner of the courtyard.
\v 22 In the four corners of the courtyard {were} enclosed courtyards, 40 in length and 30 in width. One measurement {was} for the four of them, cornered.
\v 23 And a row was in them all around, all around for the four of them; and cooking places were made under the rows all around.
\v 24 And he said to me, “These are the house of the ones boiling, which the ones serving the house shall boil there the sacrifice of the people.”
\c 47
\p
\v 1 And he returned me to the entrance of the house, and behold, waters were going out from under the threshold of the house eastward, for the face of the house {was} east. And the waters were going down from under the right shoulder of the house, from the south of the altar.
\v 2 And he brought me out {by} the way of the gate northward, and he led me around {by} the way outside to the outer gate, {by} the way facing east. And behold, waters were trickling from the right shoulder.
\p
\v 3 In the going out of the man eastward, a line {was} in his hand. And he measured 1,000 by the cubit, and he made me pass over in the waters, waters of ankles.
\v 4 And he measured 1,000, and he made me pass over in the waters, waters of knees. And he measured 1,000 and made me pass over, waters of loins.
\v 5 And he measured 1,000—a stream that I was not able to pass over, for the waters had risen, waters of swimming, a stream that could not be passed over.
\p
\v 6 And he said to me, “Have you seen, son of man?” And he led me and returned me {to} the lip of the stream.
\v 7 In my returning, then behold, on the lip of the stream {were} very many trees, from this and from this.
\v 8 And he said to me, “These waters are going out to the eastern region and will go down onto the Arabah, and they will enter to the sea. To the sea having gone forth, then the waters will be healed.
\v 9 And it will be, every living creature that swarms, to every place the two streams come there, will live. And the fish will be very many, for these waters will have come there, and they will be healed; and everything will live where the stream comes there.
\v 10 And it will be, fishermen will stand beside it; from En Gedi and to En Eglaim they will be a spreading place for nets. According to its kind their fish will be, like the fish of the Great Sea, very many.
\v 11 Its marsh and its pools will not be healed; to salt they have been given.
\v 12 And by the stream, on its lip, from this and from this, every tree of food will come up. Its leaf will not wither, and its fruit will not come to an end. In its months it will bear firstfruits, for its waters—from the sanctuary they are going out. And its fruit will be for food, and its leaf for healing.”
\p
\v 13 Thus says the Lord Yahweh, “This {is} the border {by} which you shall inherit the land for the 12 tribes of Israel. Joseph {shall have} portions.
\v 14 And you shall inherit it, a man like his brother, which I lifted up my hand to give it to your fathers. And this land will fall to you as an inheritance.
\p
\v 15 And this is the border of the land: to the side northward, from the Great Sea, the way of Hethlon, Lebo, toward Zedad;
\v 16 Hamath, Berothah, Sibraim, which {is} between the border of Damascus and between the border of Hamath, Hazer Hattikon, which {is} at the border of Hauran.
\v 17 And the border from the sea will be Hazar Enon, the border of Damascus; and the north, northward, and the border of Hamath. And {this is} the side of the north.
\v 18 And the side of the east: from between Hauran and from between Damascus and from between the Gilead and from between the land of Israel, the Jordan; from the border to the eastern sea you shall measure. And {this is} the side eastward.
\v 19 And the side of the south, southward: from Tamar to the waters of Meribah Kadesh, the wadi, to the Great Sea. And {this is} the side southward, toward the south.
\v 20 And the side of the sea: the Great Sea from the border to opposite Lebo Hamath. This is the side of the sea.
\p
\v 21 And you shall divide this land for yourselves according to the tribes of Israel.
\v 22 And it shall be, you shall cause it to fall as an inheritance for yourselves and for the sojourners, those sojourning in your midst, who have fathered sons in your midst. And they shall be for you like a native among the sons of Israel; with you they shall fall in an inheritance in the midst of the tribes of Israel.
\v 23 And it shall be in the tribe that the sojourner has sojourned with it, there you shall give his inheritance—the declaration of the Lord Yahweh.”
\c 48
\p
\v 1 And these are the names of the tribes: from the end northward, to the hand of the way of Hethlon, Lebo Hamath, Hazar Enan, the border of Damascus northward, to the hand of Hamath; and they will be for him: the side of the east {and} the sea. Dan, one {portion}.
\v 2 And on the border of Dan, from the side of the east to the side seaward: Asher, one {portion}.
\v 3 And on the border of Asher, from the side eastward and to the side seaward: Naphtali, one {portion}.
\v 4 And on the border of Naphtali, from the side eastward to the side seaward: Manasseh, one {portion}.
\v 5 And on the border of Manasseh, from the side eastward to the side seaward: Ephraim, one {portion}.
\v 6 And on the border of Ephraim, from the side of the east and to the side seaward: Reuben, one {portion}.
\v 7 And on the border of Reuben, from the side of the east to the side seaward: Judah, one {portion}.
\p
\v 8 And on the border of Judah, from the side of the east to the side seaward, will be the contribution that you will lift up: 25,000 in width, and the length like one of the portions, from the side eastward to the side seaward. And the sanctuary will be in its midst.
\v 9 The contribution that you will lift up to Yahweh: a length of 25,000 and a width of 10,000.
\v 10 And to these will be the contribution of the holiness: for the priests, northward 25,000, and seaward a width of 10,000, and eastward a width of 10,000, and southward a length of 25,000. And the sanctuary of Yahweh will be in its midst.
\v 11 For the priests, the one being made holy from the sons of Zadok, who kept my watch, who did not go astray in the going astray of the sons of Israel, just as the Levites went astray.
\p
\v 12 And there will be for them a contribution from the contribution of the land, a holy of holies, to the border of the Levites.
\v 13 And the Levites, corresponding to the border of the priests: 25,000 in length and a width of 10,000. All the length is 25,000, and the width 10,000.
\v 14 And they will not sell from it, and he will not exchange {it}, and he will not pass over the first of the land, for it is holy to Yahweh.
\p
\v 15 And the 5,000, the remainder in the width, on the face of the 25,000: it is common, for the city, for a dwelling and for pastureland. And the city will be in its midst.
\v 16 And these are its measurements: the side of the north, 4,500; and the side of the south, 4,500; and from the side of the east, 4,500; and the side seaward, 4,500.
\v 17 And there will be pastureland for the city: northward 250, and southward 250, and eastward 250, and seaward 250.
\v 18 And the remainder in the length, corresponding to the contribution of the holiness: 10,000 eastward and 10,000 seaward. And it will be corresponding to the contribution of the holiness, and its produce will be for bread for the ones serving the city.
\v 19 And the one serving the city, from all the tribes of Israel, they will serve it.
\v 20 All the contribution: 25,000 by 25,000, a square. You shall lift up the contribution of the holiness to the possession of the city.
\p
\v 21 And the remainder will be for the prince, from this and from this, for the contribution of the holiness and for the possession of the city, to the face of the 25,000 of the contribution, to the border eastward; and seaward, on the face of the 25,000, on the border seaward, corresponding to the portions, for the prince. And the contribution of the holiness and the sanctuary of the house will be in its midst.
\v 22 And from the possession of the Levites and from the possession of the city, in the midst of that will be for the prince: between the border of Judah and the between border of Benjamin it will be for the prince.
\p
\v 23 And the rest of the tribes, from the side eastward to the side seaward: Benjamin, one {portion}.
\v 24 And on the border of Benjamin, from the side eastward to the side seaward: Simeon, one {portion}.
\v 25 And on the border of Simeon, from the side eastward to the side seaward: Issachar, one {portion}.
\v 26 And on the border of Issachar, from the side eastward to the side seaward: Zebulun, one {portion}.
\v 27 And on the border of Zebulun, from the side eastward to the side seaward: Gad, one {portion}.
\v 28 And on the border of Gad, to the side of the south, southward: and the border will be from Tamar {to} the waters of Meribah Kadesh, the wadi, to the Great Sea.
\v 29 This is the land that you shall cause to fall as an inheritance for the tribes of Israel, and these are their divisions— the declaration of the Lord Yahweh.
\p
\v 30 And these are the goings out of the city: from the side of the north, 4,500 in measurement.
\v 31 And the gates of the city are according to the names of the tribes of Israel: three gates northward— the gate of Reuben, one; the gate of Judah, one; the gate of Levi, one.
\v 32 And to the side eastward, 4,500, and three gates: the gate of Joseph, one; the gate of Benjamin, one; the gate of Dan, one.
\v 33 And the side southward, 4,500 in measurement, and three gates: the gate of Simeon, one; the gate of Issachar, one; the gate of Zebulun, one.
\v 34 The side seaward, 4,500; their gates, three: the gate of Gad, one; the gate of Asher, one; the gate of Naphtali, one.
\v 35 All around: 18,000. And the name of the city from that day: “Yahweh Is There.” 